    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Manager--SOTA-Events---Operations_JR100311": {
      "title": "Manager, SOTA Events & Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Manager, SOTA Events & Operations ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Events Manager for the NKU School of the Arts is an in-person role that provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for the planning, coordination, and execution of all events across Theatre & Dance, Music, and Art & Design. This position ensures that performances, exhibitions, and programs are delivered with a high level of organization, collaboration, and professionalism, aligning with academic priorities and enhancing the visibility and reputation of the School. Serving as the central hub for event logistics, the Events Manager fosters communication across programs, supports student and faculty success, and creates a cohesive, high-quality experience for audiences, campus partners, and the broader community. Reporting to the SOTA director, the SOTA Events Manager serves as the primary point of contact and coordination for event logistics in SOTA’s venues, including the 320-seat Corbett Theatre, the Stauss Black Box Theatre, the 650-seat Greaves Concert Hall, and the SOTA Galleries as well as with external partnerships. The role requires very strong organizational and communication skills, a collaborative working style, and the ability to manage multiple simultaneous events in a vibrant performing and visual arts environment. The Manager of Galleries and Outreach (Art & Design), the Greaves Concert Hall Coordinator (Music), and the Front of House Coordinator (Music and Theatre & Dance) all report to the Events Manager and form the SOTA Events Team managing all aspects of SOTA events. ‌ Event Planning, Coordination & Academic Alignment • Develop and manage SOTA’s annual events calendar across Theatre & Dance, Music (including Music Prep), and Art & Design (including Art Prep). • Coordinate with Program Heads, directors, faculty, staff, production teams, student leaders, and campus partners to plan event requirements, schedules, logistics, and operations; lead regular SOTA Events Team meetings. • Ensure events align with NKU academic calendars, space use policies, accessibility standards, and campus safety protocols, and communicate event details to internal and external stakeholders while supporting external partnerships with SOTA leadership. Event Operations & On-Site Management • Work with SOTA’s ticketing system to input paid events, make reservations, reserve complimentary tickets, etc. • Coordinate the SOTA Events Team for on-site event management for performances, exhibitions, recitals, and special programming. • Coordinate with parking services, NKU facilities and conference services, and with Truist Arena on scheduling, timing, and overlapping event logistics Marketing, Communications & Patron Experience • Collaborate with NKU’s Marketing and Communication staff to support the creation of promotional materials, digital content, lobby displays, programs, and signage. • Collaborate with SOTA’s internal resources to ensure social media channels remain current. • Ensure event information is accurate and timely across NKU calendars, websites, and social platforms. • Ensure than event information is communicated accurately and timely across external platforms including ArtsWave, area newspapers, etc. • In collaboration with the Front of House Manager, implement strategies to enhance the patron experience and audience engagement Venue Scheduling & Resource Management • In coordination with the SOTA Events Team, oversee booking and scheduling for the Corbett Theatre, Stauss Theatre, Greaves Concert Hall, SOTA Galleries, rehearsal rooms, studios, and multipurpose spaces using NKU-approved scheduling systems. • Coordinate equipment, front-of-house resources, gallery needs, and event staffing. • Maintain inventory and organization of event-related supplies and materials including internal and external signage, etc. • Serve as liaison with NKU units such as Facilities, IT, Enrollment/Admissions (for recruitment and outreach events), Parking, Advancement, and the Office of the Provost for academic scheduling needs Budgeting, Compliance & Administrative Duties • Assist with planning, tracking, and reconciling event-related budgets. • Process event-related purchasing, work orders, and vendor payments in compliance with NKU policies. • Draft and maintain event documentation, post-event reports, and operational records. • Coordinate with the SOTA Budget Officer to transfer funds from ticketing system. 6 Student Training, Mentorship & Academic Support – 3% • Coordinate with faculty to support curricular events such as student recitals, showcases, exhibitions, and end-of-semester presentations. • Provide experiential learning opportunities related to arts management, hospitality, and production support. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: • Experience in higher education or academic arts settings. • Familiarity with theatre, concert hall, and gallery operations. • Knowledge of front-of-house management, ticketing systems, and venue scheduling software. • Supervisory experience of both teams and individuals. • Understanding of production processes in theatre, dance, music, and visual arts. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: Bachelor’s degree in arts administration, event management, theatre, music, visual arts, communications, or a related field; or equivalent experience, plus 4 years of related work experience. 4 years related management experience. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITY This position would supervise the Front of House Coordinator, Greaves Concert Hall Coordinator, and Manager of Galleries and Outreach all report to this person. Also works closely with the Programs and Production Assistant. Please provide a resume, cover letter and reference document ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Administrative-Assistant_JR100329-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Administrative Assistant ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Administrative Assistant for University Housing is responsible for the strategic management and oversight of the financial, business, and administrative operations of University Housing. This position helps to manage the budget development, some fiscal forecasting, financial analysis, procurement, revenue monitoring, and business process optimization to ensure the financial sustainability and operational effectiveness of a self-supporting auxiliary. Working closely with the Director of Housing, the Administrative Assistant serves as a fiscal advisor for University Housing and provides financial leadership that supports departmental priorities, occupancy management, student experience initiatives, and long-term strategic planning. The position ensures compliance with university, state, and regulatory financial requirements while promoting operational efficiency and sound stewardship of institutional resources. ‌ Budget Support: •Process professional development/travel documents for University Housing Leadership •Team and train other housing staff on proper process completion •Process supply orders •Initiate purchase requisitions and payments through SAP •Process and submit deposits to Student Account Services •Communicate with the staff in the processing of payment information and budget tracking, planning, and development •Serve as budget liaison when questions arise Human Resources Support: •Serve as time administrator when needed •Assist with on-boarding/off-boarding University Housing employees •Coordinate with search committees on interview scheduling/agendas and document •management of positions. •Process travel reimbursements to candidates and external service providers Administrative Support: •Assist Director of Housing with scheduling meetings •Create meeting agendas and meeting minutes •Maintain University Housing calendar, policies, and procedures documents •Plan and coordinate, in coordination with the University Housing leadership team, various housing functions and events •Assist with the creating and distribution of departmental communications •Assist in establishing and maintaining an efficient and up-to-date records management system including digital records Facilities Support: •Schedule the use of various meeting rooms available within University Housing, when needed One to three years of progressively responsible experience in budgeting or business management. •Experience with budget management systems, databases, or student information systems. •Demonstrated organizational, communication, and customer service skills. •Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. •Strong attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Please attach a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Career-Advisor_JR100167": {
      "title": "Career Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Career Advisor ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Provide direct career development services and instructional programs to students/alumni of all academic majors at NKU. Conduct related research and perform associated administrative duties. Develop and maintain relationships with students, faculty, employers and others in and around the NKU community. ‌ ​• Provide individual career and graduate/professional school-advising for students/alumni of all academic majors. Assist students seeking internships, co-ops, and/or full-time positions. Help students choosing a major/career or considering graduate/professional school. Administer and interpret career-related assessment instruments. • Prepare instructional materials on career services, career development, and various elements of the co-op/internship/job-search process. Present related orientations, workshops, and instructional programs. Teach the career planning course, CEP 101: Career Planning, as assigned. • Conduct outreach activities and serve as liaison between the Norse Network Hub and appropriate employers, NKU offices, departments, and student groups. Assist in creating newsletters and marketing materials to promote services and programs of the Norse Network Hub. • Assist in the administration of job/career fairs, on-campus recruiting, and related events. Coordinate specialized career events on campus as assigned. • Be familiar with Norse Network Hub policies, procedures, and maintain an ongoing awareness of all programs and activities. Participate in appropriate professional development activities. Assist in the day-to-day operation of the Norse Network Hub. Perform other duties as assigned. • Prepare and maintain pertinent records and reports associated with assigned responsibilities. • Develop and maintain familiarity/expertise with resources pertinent to the career interests of students. ​ KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: • Knowledge and experience advising students/clients in career development and employment issues. • Also prefer some knowledge and experience using computerized assessments such as Discover or Focus II. • Superior oral and written communication skills. • Well-developed organizational abilities with a high attention to detail. • Comfortable planning and executing events/programs. • High energy level, team-player, strong initiative, and work ethic. • Familiarity with Microsoft Office Suite software and Internet applications. • Willingness to work some extended hours, including some evenings as needed.   EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: • Bachelor's degree required • Master's degree in counseling, college student personnel, or related field strongly preferred • Required experience in a college/university career center for a minimum of 1 year • Certification and/or competency in assessments such as the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator (MBTI) and Strong Interest Inventory desired but not required. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​ ​ Valid driver’s license   required   and dependable vehicle. Some evening and weekend work   is   required . ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Environmental-Specialist_JR100315": {
      "title": "Environmental Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Environmental Specialist ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: Interns work side-by-side with CER professional staff to complete environmental restoration projects within protected natural areas in northern Kentucky. Internships last for three months with the possibility of extensions up to one year. Opportunities available year-round. Internships may be part time or full time, have whole-day work days, and are one to five days per week. Training is provided and no prior environmental restoration experience is required. Requirements: ability to lift 50lbs ability to work outside in all weather conditions, for long hours reliable transportation willingness to work with herbicides comfort encountering poison ivy, ticks, and other natural hazards ‌ This internship is for new environmental professionals, entails office and fieldwork , and promotes leadership, management, and technical skill development. Field activities may include leading small invasive plant removal crews (which includes herbicide record-keeping), stream and macroinvertebrate assessments, conservation easement inspections, sediment and erosion control, and other conservation tasks. Many interns may learn to operate compact construction equipment such as Bobcat track loaders and excavators.  Office activities include preparing plans and/or monitoring reports for restoration projects under the direction of CER staff, and co-presenting them to regulatory agency personnel for review and approval. Interns should be confident working with ArcPro and ArcOnline, have good organizational and technical writing skills, and be able to work well independently.  ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ability to lift 50lbs ability to work outside in all weather conditions, for long hours reliable transportation willingness to work with herbicides comfort encountering poison ivy, ticks, and other natural hazards"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Academic-Secretary_JR100274": {
      "title": "Academic Secretary",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Secretary ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The academic secretary maintains the electronic database and paper records for the Upward Bound Program. They keep accurate books of program accounts and reconcile the program’s purchasing each month. They publish newsletters, brochures, and grant materials. They complete forms, memoranda, and requests to sustain daily operations of the program. They serve as a receptionist to visitors. Check and update social media weekly. ‌ Description of Duties: Initiate paperwork for ensuring personnel hires, purchasing supplies and equipment, travel authorizations. Use Workday for these processes. Reconcile the program's purchases and record-keeping (stipends, credit cards, etc). Update the program's database and improve the program's documents. Use of computer and knowledge of Microsoft Software for program essentials Maintain filing system in hard copy and electronic forms Assist Program Director in preparation for budget and federal annual reporting processes. Assist with auditing processes and tracking alumni. Checking and responding to emails about program Update calendars for staff members and help with the initiation of activities for the program. Occassionally making reservations on and off campus. Maintain office supplies and inventory Open and Distribute Mail Create infographics for the Program for social media posts and publications Requirements:  High School Diploma/GED is required but some college to a college degree is preferred.  Two years of related work or experience is preferred ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Director--Annual-Leadership-Giving_JR100321": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Annual Leadership Giving",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director, Annual Leadership Giving ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Director of Annual Leadership Giving is a key member of the Annual Giving team and is responsible for building meaningful relationships with alumni, parents, friends, and donors through personalized outreach and engagement strategies. This position manages a portfolio of leadership annual giving prospects and donors, with an emphasis on identifying, cultivating, and soliciting individuals capable of upgrading their current level of support or making annual gifts at leadership giving levels of $1,000 - $50,000. Working within a donor-centered fundraising model, the Assistant Director leverages a variety of communication channels, to strengthen constituent engagement and inspire philanthropic support. The position serves as an ambassador for Northern Kentucky University, effectively communicating the university's mission, priorities, and impact while connecting donor interests with institutional needs. Success in this role requires strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills, comfort with high-volume personalized outreach, and the ability to manage multiple constituent interactions simultaneously. The Assistant Director must be comfortable with utilizing fundraising databases, communication platforms, and emerging engagement technologies to advance prospects through the donor pipeline and achieve annual fundraising goals. ‌ Manage a portfolio of prospects and donors, developing and executing individualized cultivation and solicitation strategies to increase engagement and philanthropic support in the $1,000–$50,000 giving range. Conduct outreach through phone calls, email, text messaging, video messages, virtual meetings, and personal visits. Maintain regular contact to strengthen relationships, increase participation, secure gift upgrades, and achieve fundraising goals. Qualify prospects for leadership annual giving opportunities and identify individuals with the capacity and inclination for increased philanthropic investment using predictive analytics and upgrade scoring models. Identify, cultivate, and solicit prospects for Founders’ Day match and challenge gifts to support annual participation and fundraising goals. Develop engagement, impact and solicitation strategy for high net wealth Parents. Maintain accurate and timely records of prospect activity, qualifications, proposals, solicitations, and outcomes in the Blackbaud Raiser's Edge NXT database. Develop a comprehensive understanding of NKU’s priorities, philanthropic opportunities, student impact initiatives, and alumni engagement programs. Use this knowledge to align donor interests with institutional needs, deepen donor relationships, and strengthen the pipeline for future major gift support. Support Annual Giving campaigns, projects, and special initiatives, including Founders’ Day and other strategic fundraising efforts. Serve a backup to Engagement Center manager, occasionally requiring evening hours. Bachelor's degree in communications, marketing, business, project management, nonprofit management, or a related field. The ideal candidate will have experience in consultative sales, fundraising, customer service, or business development, with the ability to cultivate relationships, effectively communicate value, overcome objections, and secure commitments. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong collaboration and relationship-building skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Office. Strong editing, proofreading, and quality-control skills. Experience with Raisers’ Edge NXT, Give Campus Online and GCGO software a plus. Please attach a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Drivers License and reliable vehicle required."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Program-Coordinator_JR100244-1": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Program Coordinator ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: Support IHI's K-12 pathway programs as a Program Coordinator, helping coordinate stakeholder communications and program logistics under the direction of the Program Manager. ‌ The Program Coordinator plays a key support role in advancing the Institute for Health Innovation's K-12 pathway programs, working under the direction of the Program Manager. This position helps coordinate communications and maintain strong working relationships across team members, community partners, private entities, and public organizations. The Program Coordinator supports the development, implementation, and ongoing operation of programming by helping execute the plans and initiatives set by the Program Manager, in alignment with IHI's goals. This role is instrumental in keeping day-to-day IHI activities running smoothly and on schedule. Specific duties include: Prepare materials for events and K-12 pathway programs, as directed by the Program Manager; record and track data related to K-12 pathway programs; Coordinate day-of logistics for K-12 pathway programs under the direction of the Program Manager; Assist the Program Manager with research on new pathway programs and help execute implementation tasks as assigned; Support annual assessment of programs by compiling data and materials to inform the Program Manager's evaluation of effectiveness and best practices; The ideal candidate will be comfortable interacting with a wide range of constituencies — including faculty, staff, students, alumni, and community members — while supporting the broader stakeholder relationships managed by the Program Manager. Please attach a resume, cover letter and document with contact information for references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Part-time-Faculty-Chemistry---Biochemistry_JR100319": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty Chemistry & Biochemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-17\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part-time Faculty Chemistry & Biochemistry ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Northern Kentucky University is seeking to create a database of potential part-time instructors who are qualified to teach courses in one or more of the following disciplines: While we welcome teaching expertise in all areas, our most common needs are in the general chemistry sequence (CHE 120, CHE 120L, CHE 121L, CHE 121L), physiological chemistry (CHE 115, CHE 115L), and organic chemistry laboratory (CHE 310L, CHE 311L). ‌ Teaching responsibilities involve: Teaching a two or three-contact hour course during scheduled course times. Creating a syllabus with a timeline of classes for students. Providing times to meet students outside of class (office hours; virtual or face-to-face). Managing course content for students through Canvas Managing mid-term and final grades though the MyNKU online grading system. Also, under the direction of the Academic Department Chair and in consultation with the course coordinator: Develop and manage syllabus materials. The faculty is responsible for selecting and compiling tests, assignments and/or online discussion exercises that permit measurement of performance relative to standardized learning objectives. Coordinate courseware and curriculum with academic department chair. The faculty is responsible for reviewing any textbook and other courseware changes with the academic department chair and other full-time faculty teaching the course. Facilitate class instruction. The faculty is responsible for teaching the assigned class in accordance with learning objectives and session plan outlines The faculty is expected to administer evaluations of student performance based on course deliverables and course rubrics.   All applicants must have a minimum of a Master’s Degree or equivalent in Chemistry or a closely related discipline. Please submit your application with a cover letter, vitae, and the names of at least three professional references. Application materials will be used to create a database of potential part time faculty. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/AmeriCorps-Kentucky-College-Coach_JR100198": {
      "title": "AmeriCorps Kentucky College Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-14\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: AmeriCorps Kentucky College Coach ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: Kentucky College Coaches are AmeriCorps State and National members that assist high school students with selecting, applying to, and being accepted to a college or career of their choice. This involves hosting school-wide activities and mentoring core students from each grade level (9th-12th grade), as designated by the member’s site supervisor. These priority core students will be students who: 1) will likely get through high school, but who are unlikely to go to college 2) would be first-generation college attendees and/or 3) are from low-income families. ‌ Duration:   September 1, 2026 – June 31, 2027 (10   months)*   Living Allowance/Pay:   $ 1,85 0 per month in living allowance, less   FICA   and other applicable taxes   Benefits:   Assistance applying for healthcare and childcare, education award of a maximum of $5,176.50 per service term upon fulfillment of contract, federal student loan forbearance eligibility, and professional development   Minimum Qualifications :   Associate’s   degree* (preferred), excellent communication and organizational skills, and mentoring experience.    More Information:    Efforts to reach both the whole-school population and the priority students should be measurable in terms of the following:   Number of priority students assigned to a Kentucky College Coach who persist in the program throughout the school year   Number of students graduating from high school    Number of students entering post-secondary institutions   Number of students   that are   career ready      The Kentucky College Coach should work to help the school   attain   the following benchmarks:   Number of students reaching college readiness benchmarks in math and reading as measured by the 11 th   grade ACT   Number of students applying to colleg e     Number of students filing the FAFSA   Number of students moving from high school and accessing remedial courses during the first year of college       Methods the Kentucky College Coach will employ in mentoring can include any of the following (as   deemed   appropriate by   the school site supervisor):   Helping students in career planning   Helping students with time and organizational skills    Recruiting volunteers within the community to   assist   with career awareness   Assisting   with classroom instruction by embedding college planning materials among core content   Assisting   teachers and   school   counselors to develop effective tutoring plans for students who need academic   assistance   and linking students to volunteers in the community and at local colleges for tutoring   Mentoring students about high school course   selection   and placement testing scores which can lead to successful college admission   Helping students develop financial literacy skills   Incorporating college-bound curriculum within the site school   Assisting   with family nights, as related to college admission   Other types of mentoring   based   on the needs of students and the direction of school staff and policy.   ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Members must be a U.S. Citizen, U.S. national, or legal permanent resident alien ."
    },
