    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Police-Officer_JR100007": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-07\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Police Officer ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Job Description Summary The university police officer is a member of the University Police Department, which serves and protects the campus community. The officer is responsible for maintaining a positive relationship with the university community; maintaining a secure environment; mitigating safety hazards; being observant and responding to actual and suspected criminal activity on campus; controlling and regulating traffic; and investigating security, safety, crime, and traffic incidents. The university police officer is dedicated to educating, mentoring, and contributing to the success of the university community. ‌ ​ Primary Responsibilities ​​Communicating with supervisors, peers, and all stakeholders in a courteous, culturally adroit manner that models the University Police core values, while providing an outstanding customer service experience.  ​Patrolling assigned areas on foot, bicycle, or motor vehicle.  ​Promptly, clearly, and concisely completing a variety of written incident, offense, and ancillary reports in a grammatically correct manner and in accordance with established best practices.  ​Responding to emergency alarms and dispatched calls for service.  ​Observing and responding to actual and suspected criminal activity.  ​Deterring crime and arresting violators as prescribed by Kentucky Revised Statutes.​  Qualifications: ​​High School Diploma required; Bachelor’s Degree preferred.  ​Must be 21 years of age at the time of appointment.  ​A valid driver’s license is required.  ​Any candidate who is offered this position will be required to undergo a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law.​  Successful candidates will have excellent interpersonal and communication skills. In addition, the candidate will have positive work and/or life experiences interacting and building strong relationships with people from lots of backgrounds and communities. Officers must also be willing to listen, learn, and seek opportunities to teach while actively supporting and upholding the mission and values of Northern Kentucky University. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​ ​ The selected candidate will   be required   to work 12-hour rotating shifts. Night, weekend, and holiday work   is   required . ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Create-Position--Assistant-Professor-BSN-Nursing-Tenure-Track_JR100407": {
      "title": "Create Position: Assistant Professor BSN Nursing-Tenure Track",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Create Position: Assistant Professor BSN Nursing-Tenure Track ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The School of Nursing invites applications for the tenure track Assistant Professor level position. Faculty responsibilities will include teaching in the BSN tracks, strong commitment to service, active engagement in scholarship, and general academic advising/career advising. All faculty must be prepared to plan and teach courses within their area of expertise. This includes developing (or using provided syllabus) for the classes assigned. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic, lab and clinical. ‌ Specific responsibilities include: Plan, teach, and evaluate lectures or activities within the course. Assure instructional excellence and innovation in course presentation. Remain current in the discipline through research and attendance at professional continuing education seminars. Serve on committees as assigned and attend faculty, departmental, and other meetings as necessary. Advise students throughout the semester. Provide tutoring to students upon request. Maintain office hours to be accessible and available to students and staff. Review textbooks/resources in the discipline and place orders according to the University schedule. Maintain grades and submit mid-term and/or final grades through My NKU by the University deadlines. Work cooperatively with the faculty team including adjunct clinical faculty. Contribute to scholarship or creative activities within the field of nursing or related field. Education Doctorate in nursing or related field. Two years of experience in clinical practice within the past five years required. Must have ability to teach across all BSN levels. Must have strong pathopharmacology knowledge and clinical decision making with the ability to thread nursing concepts into all assigned courses. Previous academic teaching experience preferred. Must possess a valid unencumbered nursing license. Licensure in KY and Ohio required or Multi-state Please include: Teaching Philosophy Cover letter CV References Scholarship plan ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Cybersecurity-and-Information-Technology-Assistant-Professor_JR100406": {
      "title": "Cybersecurity and Information Technology Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Cybersecurity and Information Technology Assistant Professor ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Faculty job profile with those of academic rank of Assistant Professor ‌ The School of Computing and Analytics (SCA) at Northern Kentucky University (NKU) invites applications for one full-time faculty position in Cybersecurity and Information Technology at the rank of Assistant Professor (tenure-track) beginning August 2027. Salary and benefits are competitive. We seek candidates with teaching and research expertise in cybersecurity. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, cybersecurity risk management, AI for cybersecurity, digital forensics, ethical hacking, threat modeling and incident response, software security, and data/information privacy. The position will primarily contribute to our B.S. and M.S. programs in Cybersecurity and IT, with potential contributions to other programs such as Computer Science and Applied Software Engineering. Learn more about the Cybersecurity and Information Technology programs at https://www.nku.edu/informatics/schools/sca/programs/cit/index.html NKU has been designated a National Center for Academic Excellence (CAE) in Cyber Defense by the National Security Agency (NSA) and the U.S. Department of Homeland Security. As the only CAE in the Northern Kentucky / Greater Cincinnati region with both undergraduate and graduate programs in cybersecurity, NKU plays a central role in the area’s cybersecurity education and workforce development. NKU is also the only CAE in Kentucky to host an NSA/NSF GenCyber grant program. Each fall, NKU hosts its Cybersecurity Symposium , a signature event that attracts broad participation from the Northern Kentucky and Cincinnati communities. NKU’s B.S. and M.S. in Cybersecurity are high-quality programs that provide students with strong academic preparation and meaningful opportunities to engage with faculty inside and outside the classroom. NKU’s CyberDefense student team has also excelled in regional and national competitions, giving faculty valuable opportunities to mentor and collaborate with talented, highly engaged students. NKU’s CyberDefense student team has excelled in regional and national competitions, providing faculty with meaningful opportunities to mentor and collaborate with an energetic and growing student population. The SCA is part of the College of Informatics (COI) ( informatics.nku.edu ) and is housed in Griffin Hall, a landmark high-tech building. The school offers multiple degrees and operates as a combination of three program clusters: Computer Science & Software Engineering (CS&SE), Cybersecurity & Information Technology (CYS&IT), and Information Systems & Analytics (IS&A). More information about the SCA is available also at https://www.nku.edu/informatics/schools/sca/index.html Teaching: Develop and teach courses in both face-to-face and online formats. The standard teaching load is three courses per semester for tenure-track Assistant Professors (including at least two upper-level courses). Tenure-track faculty may teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Research: Maintain an active research agenda in cybersecurity and/or information technology, with emphasis on projects that engage undergraduate and graduate students in scholarly activities. Service: Contribute to the School, College, and University through committee work and professional engagement. Faculty are also expected to support initiatives such as the annual Cybersecurity Symposium and student organizations and events in cybersecurity and IT. On-campus presence: This is not a remote position . The successful candidate will be required to relocate to the Northern Kentucky / Greater Cincinnati area. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Cybersecurity, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered. Application materials should be submitted electronically at https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External Please include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching interests Statement of research interests List of three references with complete contact information Priority will be given to applications received by November 1, 2026 . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Questions concerning this position should be addressed to: Dr. Shahid Noor, noors2@nku.edu All offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. NKU’s vision is that we will be nationally recognized for being a student-ready, regionally engaged university that empowers diverse learners for economic and social mobility. Our core values place emphasis on our culture of excellence, creativity, innovation, and collegiality. Your cover letter and/or teaching statement should show, as a faculty member at NKU, how you will contribute to our core values and our strategic framework, especially in how you will contribute to student success and belonging. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Faculty---Chase-College-of-Law_JR100378": {
      "title": "Faculty - Chase College of Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Faculty - Chase College of Law ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Faculty job profile with those of academic rank of Assistant Professor in the interest area of Federal Income Taxation and Taxation of Business Entities, Trusts & Estates, and Legal Writing ‌ Northern Kentucky University Salmon P. Chase College of Law invites applications for two tenure-track positions beginning in the fall of 2027. Among the curricular areas of interest for those positions are Federal Income Taxation and Taxation of Business Entities, Trusts & Estates, and Legal Writing. The ideal candidates will have excellent academic credentials, the ability to produce high-quality scholarship, and a strong commitment to both teaching and student success. Interested candidates must submit a cover letter and resume/CV (can upload to the same document box). Inquiries can be submitted to Toula Papakirk at papakirks1@nku.edu . ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Professor-Instrumental-Music-Education_JR100397": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Choral/Vocal Music Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor Choral/Vocal Music Education ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The School of the Arts at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in Choral/Vocal Music Education at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning August 2027. We seek a dynamic and collaborative educator committed to excellence in teaching, service, and scholarship. ‌ Primary Responsibilities : Teach undergraduate courses in music education and choral music education, which will include methods, pedagogy, supervision of student teachers, and other courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Teach undergraduate courses in a secondary area of expertise. Courses may include: applied lessons, music history, music theory, ensemble conducting, or aural skills. Coordinate the choral music education program and collaborate with faculty across performance and education areas. Engage in recruitment efforts for the music education program through fostering positive relationships with public school music educators and their programs. Demonstrate a trajectory of active research, scholarship, and/or creative activity. Participate in service to the program, college, and profession. Advise undergraduate students and contribute to curriculum development. Required Qualifications : PhD, DME, or DMA in Music Education (ABD considered). Minimum of three years of successful teaching experience in K–12 choral music. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Record of scholarship that includes an established or emerging portfolio of publications and/or presentations at state/regional/national conferences. Familiarity with current pedagogy, trends, and technologies in music education. Preferred Qualifications: Experience supervising student teachers or coordinating field experiences. Collegiate-level teaching experience. Record of scholarly activity in music education. Application Materials : (All documents can be added in the same documents box) A letter of application outlining the candidate’s qualifications for this position, including their primary and secondary area(s) of expertise. Curriculum Vitae A professional teaching philosophy that includes a statement addressing how the candidate’s work would contribute to NKU’s core values and empower diverse learners. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Public-Safety-Officer--68-NE-_JR100405": {
      "title": "University Resource Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: University Resource Officer ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The University Resource Officer is a seasonal or part-time member of the UPD team (generally August through May) with responsibilities for providing law enforcement services to the campus community. Candidates must be eligible for appointment under K.R.S. 164.952, including retirement from a KPPA administered system with at least 20 years of service credit and in good standing. This position is for 1500 hours typically worked from August through May. ‌ ​ ​ Communicating with supervisors, peers, and all stakeholders in a courteous,   culturally adroit   manner that models the University Police core values, while providing an outstanding customer service experience.   ​ Patrolling assigned areas on foot, bicycle, or motor vehicle .   ​ Promptly, clearly, and concisely completing a variety of written   incident ,   offense , and ancillary reports in a grammatically correct manner and   in accordance with   established best practices .   ​ Responding to emergency alarms and dispatched calls for service .   ​ Observing and responding to actual and suspected criminal activity .   ​ Deterring crime and arresting violators   as prescribed by   Kentucky Revised Statutes . ​ POSTED SALARY: $42.00 per hour plus KLEFPF EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: ﻿The University Resource Officer is a seasonal or part-time member of the UPD team (generally August through May) with responsibilities for providing law enforcement services to the campus community.  Candidates must be eligible for appointment under K.R.S. 164.952, including retirement from a KPPA administered system with at least 20 years of service credit and in good standing.  ​ Any candidate who is offered this position will   be required   to undergo a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. ​     KNOWLEDGE,   SKILLS   AND ABILITIES   (KSAs ): ​ ​ S uccessful candidates will have excellent interpersonal and communication skills. In addition, the candidate will have positive work and/or life experiences interacting and building strong relationships with people from diverse backgrounds and communities. Officers must also be willing to listen, learn, and seek opportunities to teach while actively supporting and upholding the mission and values of Northern Kentucky University.   ​ The successful candidate will   be required   to   demonstrate   competent solo patrol and investigative abilities by satisfying the knowledge and performance-based benchmarks   set forth in   the supervised Field Training Observation & Evaluation program. ​   ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​ ​ The selected candidate will   be required   to work 12-hour rotating shifts. Night, weekend, and holiday work   is   required . ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Academic-Coordinator_JR100408": {
      "title": "Academic Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Coordinator ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: This position provides comprehensive administrative support to the College of Health & Human Services (CHHS) and its academic programs. Responsibilities include supporting the college’s financial management, accounts payable, billing, and reporting functions, as well as providing dedicated administrative and academic support to select programs and centers. ‌ Administrative Support of New Hire Process, Faculty Credentialing, and Personnel Documentation/Processes Responsible for processing confidential pay & personnel (PAPS, etc.) Responsible for setting up faculty/instructor data & credentialing materials in Faculty Success. Support GA hiring support for the college. Oversight for confidential departmental, student, and faculty files. Responsible for processing Separation PAPs and related paperwork/ electronic inputs for Faculty & Staff positions. College recruit and events support. External partners support. Administrative support of Financial Management, Bill Pay, and Reporting Functions Responsible for general financial management functions, including grants and foundation accounts. Responsible for processing Travel Requests and Expense Reports, Purchasing Supplies and reconciling ProCards, and Time Administration. Ensures compliance with all NKU guidelines. Key Designee for CHHS (Key requests, returns, audits, etc.) Responsible for directly or as the backup resource for bill payment, purchase requisitions, budget transfers, revenue transfers, vendor setup, revenue collection & bursar deposits, reconciliation of accounts, and other financial administration related duties. Responsible for and assist the Business Officer with CHHS Reporting. Responsible for directly or as the backup resource for the coordination of grant accounts and associated paperwork with faculty and other CHHS Staff. Oversight of departmental equipment/ furniture/ computer inventory (including annual reconciliations, tagging, and upgrade/replacement processes) Support other responsibilities as needed. Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree and 2 years of work experience required General business and computer skills, with proficiency in MS Office Suite (especially Excel), Adobe, and Canva. SAP and Workday experience is helpful, yet not mandatory. Require good time management, basic math skills, interpersonal and communication skills, as well as the ability to adapt to change quickly. Good data skills, keen attention to detail , and a very high accuracy rate. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​ ​ Indoor desk work ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Academic-Advisor_JR100355": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Advisor ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The advisor will meet with undergraduate students during scheduled and walk-in appointments; communicates with undergraduate students on advising issues; participates in Master Advising professional development training; generates and disseminates student reports; works with myNKU/SAP system to review student information and help students register for classes; and serves on committees within the College of Education and across the university. ‌ Provide academic advising to students majoring in the College of Education undergraduate programs Engage in professional communication (i.e., fact-to-face meetings, email, phone calls, Zoom, etc.) with undergraduate students on advising issues and questions Participate in professional collaboration with other advisors and colleagues in the College of Education Provide assistance to students with regard to placement, transfer, graduation, certification and other degree-path issues to ensure student success Collaborate with colleagues on admissions, orientation, recruitment and retention events sponsored by Academic Affairs and Student Affairs Prepare advising files for students ready to enter student teaching that will be reviewed by the Director of Educational Placements Generate and disseminate data reports from myNKU/SAP, Navigate, Watermark SLL and other university sources of information Serve on College of Education and NKU committees as appropriate to the duties/responsibilities of the position Bachelor's degree required; preferred qualifications are a master's degree in College Student Personnel, Counseling, Communication, Education or other academic discipline with experience in academic advising. Minimum of two years academic advising experience in a higher education setting preferred. Applicants must list a minimum of three references as well as a resume and cover letter. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---MSN--Core_JR100418": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - MSN  Core",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor - MSN Core ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Teaching Professor is responsible for coordinating, leading, and teaching courses in the MSN program. The MSN Faculty upholds academic integrity, follows standards of practice, and collaborates with the all MSN and SON faculty to ensure curriculum alignment with CCNE Essentials and the national standards applicable to the assigned track. The role supports graduate preparation for national certification eligibility in the APRN, NEL, or NED track, fosters program effectiveness, and promotes a student-centered, high-quality learning environment. ‌ Organizational Relationship: Workload assigned by the Associate Director/MSN Program Director and SON Director Evaluated annually by the Associate School Director and/or SON Director and with input from peer faculty Maintain regular, proactive communication with MSN Faculty and Program Director regarding course operations, student concerns, and any emerging issues, ensuring alignment with program expectations and timely resolution. Program Leadership: Actively engage in SON, MSN program, course, and university meetings, as designated by the SON Director and Associate Director/MSN Program director to support shared governance and program effectiveness. Collaborate regularly with other MSN Faculty to address MSN curriculum, course content, grading practices, student concerns, and faculty or university-related matters. Escalate unresolved issues to the MSN Program Director following appropriate communication pathways. Contribute to program success through participation in activities related to student admission, progression, and orientation, as well as curriculum review and enhancement for students enrolled in or applying to the MSN program. Ensure alignment with CCNE Standards, the national competencies applicable to the assigned track (NONPF for APRN; AONL and NLN for NEL and NED), and other professional standards as appropriate. Faculty Leadership : Maintain an active presence and engagement throughout the MSN program by monitoring responsiveness, grading practices, and interactions with students. Collaboratively review and discuss student assignments receiving a grade of 80% or below to ensure timely academic support and consistency in evaluation. Plan, teach, manage, and evaluate lectures and course activities while ensuring instructional excellence and innovation in content delivery. Review course materials, including readings, textbooks, and learning resources, to ensure alignment with current evidence-based practice, CCNE Standards, the national competencies applicable to the assigned track (NONPF for APRN; AONL and NLN for NEL and NED), and other professional standards as appropriate and communicate any necessary updates to the applicable MSN Track Coordinator(s) to maintain curricular relevance and accuracy. Collaborates closely with the MSN Program Director/Associate Director and MSN faculty to maintain the quality of courses and overall program effectiveness while fostering an enriching learning experience for students. Other duties include: Be accessible and available to students, supervisor, staff and colleagues during NKU operation hours (8:00 am – 4:30 pm EST). Serve on SON and program committees as assigned and attend SON, program, and other meetings in person or virtually; be an active participate in SON, program, and university needs. Education Doctoral degree in Nursing or related field required. For APRN track positions, an Advanced Practice Certification in a nurse practitioner specialty (FNP, AGACNP, PMHNP). For NEL and NED track positions, MSN in nursing with graduate preparation in nursing leadership/administration or nursing education, respectively Qualifications: Minimum of two years of clinical nursing practice required. Must possess an active and unencumbered registered nursing (RN) license in State of residence and, for APRN track positions, an advanced practice license For APRN track positions, at least five years of full-time, past and current direct patient care as an APRN in the designated specialty area. For NEL and NED track positions, comparable full-time professional experience in nursing leadership/administration or nursing education, as applicable Previous graduate- level teaching required Previous online teaching experience required Experience or expertise with course content  Pass pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law Professional Expectations: Maintain active unencumbered RN licensure and, for APRN track positions, APRN certification/licensure; NEL and NED faculty maintain any certifications relevant to their track Maintain current knowledge of professional discipline and educational methodologies through continuing professional development For APRN track positions, maintain part-time clinical practice as needed to maintain APRN certification/licensure; ensure clinical practice (max release is one day weekly) does not interfere with faculty duties Maintain current knowledge of program policies, procedures, and student progress Adhere to faculty professional standards as delineated in the NKU Faculty Handbook Utilize nku.edu email for ALL course communications – students are required to do the same Teach and precept as needed to meet program needs Required Training: Completes ‘Best Practices for Online Teaching’ Canvas course as assigned Completes required Faculty Development courses annually Complete Clinical systems training currently used in program (i.e., Medatrax) Please include: RN license report (from NURSYS) APRN Certificate (as appropriate) CV Teaching Philosophy Cover letter References ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-and-Clinical-Coordinator--Cardiovascular-Perfusion-Program_JR100417": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor and Clinical Coordinator, Cardiovascular Perfusion Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor and Clinical Coordinator, Cardiovascular Perfusion Program ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University’s (NKU) School of Allied Health, within the College of Health & Human Services, is seeking a fulltime Clinical Coordinator and faculty member to teach in the Master of Science in Cardiovascular Perfusion program. NKU, a growing metropolitan university located 7 miles from Cincinnati, is a university known to its faculty and students for its commitment to student success. The clinical coordinator will have teaching responsibilities and will oversee clinical aspects of the program in collaboration with the program director, including the development of relationships with clinical partners to provide excellence in cardiovascular perfusion education opportunities. The ideal candidate for this position will be a perfusionist with a strong science and research background with teaching experience with the ability to teach across the perfusion curriculum, to include anatomy and physiology, pathophysiology, pharmacology, research methods and oversee research capstone projects. This position will also require aspects of service and commitment not only to the program, but also to the College of Health & Human Services and the university by serving on various committees when needed. This is a 12-month non-tenure track renewable faculty position at the rank of assistant teaching professor. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Teach face-to-face courses in the program, as assigned; a limited number of courses may be online, but face-to-face teaching is required Engage in student recruitment, selection, guidance, instruction, and evaluation. Support the program director in accomplishing outcomes related to planning, implementation, and evaluation of the program. Assist the program director in course development. Participate in the community advisory committee for the program and various other service activities across multiple levels (program, school, college, and university. Help guide the program to ensure alignment with the University’s strategic priorities of retention, graduation and overall student success. Communicate with current clinical sites and preceptors to assist in coordinating clinical contracts. Participate in various committee and service activities across multiple levels, including program, school, college and university. Recruit and maintain clinical sites, coordinate clinical contracts and obtain qualified preceptors at each clinical facility. Establish and maintain working relationships with staff within the clinical sites. Minimum Education & Qualifications Master’s degree (doctorate preferred) from an accredited institution recognized by the US Secretary of Education at the time the degree was conferred, in perfusion, and an education in related sciences such as biology, anatomy and physiology, biochemistry, pharmacology, exercise physiology, kinesiology. Minimum of five (5) years of professional experience as a perfusionist Minimum of 3 years pedagogical teaching experience (or instructional methodology) relevant to science courses within an academic setting. Highly developed interpersonal communication and organizational skills. Ability to create and maintain collegial relationships with internal and external team members. Commitment to the mission of NKU, College of Health and Human Services, and Program. Additional qualifications include: Active engagement in professional organizations. Any candidate who is offered this position will be required to go through a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. NKU’s vision is that we will be nationally recognized for being a student-ready, regionally engaged university that empowers diverse learners for economic and social mobility. Our core values place emphasis on our culture of excellence, creativity, innovation, and collegiality. Your cover letter and/or teaching statement should show, as a faculty member at NKU, how you will contribute to our core values and our strategic framework, especially in how you will contribute student success and belonging. Please include: Teaching Philosophy Cover letter CV References ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Tenure-Track--Assistant-Professor-Bachelor-in-Social-Work-Program_JR100415-1": {
      "title": "Tenure Track- Assistant Professor Bachelor in Social Work Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track- Assistant Professor Bachelor in Social Work Program ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The School of Social Work invites applications for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor position. The faculty member in this position will teach in both our BSW & MSW programs, including in-person, hybrid, and online courses. We seek a colleague who will contribute to a collegial and collaborative work environment and maintain a presence on campus, with a strong commitment to service and active engagement in scholarship. Preference will be given to candidates with experience teaching across the BSW and MSW curricula, including foundational and applied research courses and practice-oriented courses. ‌ Specific responsibilities include: Faculty members are expected to engage in teaching, scholarship, and service while demonstrating commitment to social work values and competencies in alignment with the NASW Code of Ethics and CSWE accreditation standards. Develop and deliver engaging, student-centered courses across the undergraduate and graduate curricula, including in-person, hybrid, and online courses. Engage in service that contributes to the University, the College of Health and Human Services, the School of Social Work, the social work profession, and the larger community (regional, national, and/or global). Contribute to the regular CSWE reaffirmation cycles for the BSW and MSW programs. Actively engage in scholarship activities, including peer-reviewed publications and presentations at a national and/or international level. Education/Qualifications: Required qualifications: MSW from a CSWE-accredited program. PhD in social work or a related field (ABD considered with confirmed completion date). Experience teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in online and in-person formats. Preferred qualifications: Minimum of two years post-MSW practice experience. MSW-level licensure (e.g. CSW, LCSW, LISW). Experience teaching foundational and applied research courses. Experience teaching practice-oriented courses. Experience conducting and disseminating scholarly research. Experience with or demonstrated interest in community engagement. Please include: Cover letter CV Names and contact information for 3 professional references  Teaching philosophy (2 page maximum) Writing sample (e.g. published manuscript, book chapter, chapter from dissertation) Copies of graduate transcripts (unofficial copies accepted at this initial stage) ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Lifeguard-Specialist--Staff-_JR100427": {
      "title": "Lifeguard Specialist (Staff)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Lifeguard Specialist (Staff) ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: The Lifeguard Specialist position supports the recruitment, training, certification, and ongoing coverage of aquatics staff. ‌ This position provides additional capacity to conduct swim tests, teach lifeguard certification courses, assist with in-service training, and support daily lifeguard coverage and facility operations. The role will strengthen staff preparedness, maintain required safety standards, and help ensure consistent and reliable aquatics operations. Qualifications : Must have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must be responsible and reliable. Must obtain CPR Instructor certification within first 3 months. Lifeguard certification required. Must obtain Lifeguard Instructor certification within first 3 months. Swim Instructor certification preferred. Work Schedule and Pay :   $15/hour for up to 25 hours per week (paid bi-weekly). University holidays and closures are observed. ‌ Posted Salary: $15/hour ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Biological-Sciences_JR100446": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor – Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor – Biological Sciences ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a Renewable Assistant Teaching Professor position to teach in-person, undergraduate courses in Human Nutrition and in Anatomy and Physiology. ‌ The Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a Renewable Assistant Teaching Professor position beginning Fall 2027. Primary teaching responsibilities will include in-person lecture courses in Human Nutrition as well as in-person lecture and laboratory courses in Human Anatomy and Physiology. Online sections of these courses may also be part of teaching responsibilities, depending on department need. Other courses may be assigned based on the candidate’s background and preference and department needs. The faculty member will be responsible for coordinating multiple sections of Human Nutrition. Student career mentoring responsibilities and departmental service are also required. Candidates should incorporate innovative, hands-on, dynamic, active-learning methods into their courses and keep current on new teaching strategies and technologies. Candidates should demonstrate commitment and/or experience promoting and fostering a learning environment that is supportive of individuals from diverse backgrounds. A minimum of a master’s degree in Nutrition, Physiology, Medicine, or a related discipline is required. Teaching experience in Nutrition is preferred. Experience with Human Anatomy and Physiology in both laboratory and lecture is encouraged. Online teaching experience is valued. Candidates should be strongly committed to teaching at the undergraduate level. To Apply: Submit a single PDF to JR100446 Assistant Teaching Professor - Biological Sciences containing: 1) a cover letter specifically addressing experience and qualifications, 2) a statement of teaching philosophy, including a discussion on use of evidence-based instructional practices in the classroom in past or future classes and strategies for reaching students of different backgrounds, 3) a brief statement of professional goals, 4) a current curriculum vitae, 5) unofficial graduate transcripts, and 6) contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Questions should be directed to Dr. Lauren Williamson (williamsol6@nku.edu). ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Business-Analyst-II_JR100459": {
      "title": "Business Analyst II",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Business Analyst II ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Business Systems Analyst II utilizes experience and systems knowledge to solve complex problems. Individuals in this role shall specialize in Human Resources and Payroll and have the ability to provide consultative assistance to other functional areas at the university such a Finance and Student. Other responsibilities include writing specifications; performing systems and data analysis; implementing and modifying business processes and configurations; and approving detailed test plans. The Business Systems Analyst II may also be required to provide technical configuration, security administration, testing, and support maintenance of NKU's enterprise management system (Workday); and may oversee development assignments across multiple platforms, including Workday integrations and reporting tools. ‌ Supports functional areas including reviewing project opportunity proposals, writing specifications, performing business process and data analysis, configuring and modifying Workday business processes and tenant setup, approving detailed test plans, and managing small to medium projects. Provides technical configuration, security group/role administration, testing, and support maintenance of NKU's Workday tenant, including business process configuration, condition rules, and notifications. Collaborates with developers, integration teams, and subject matter experts to establish technical vision, support EIBs/Workday Studio integrations, and analyze tradeoffs between usability and performance needs. Works closely with and serves as the primary backup for the area manager. Provides end-user support, troubleshooting, and training on Workday functionality; develops training materials and job aides for business process changes. Provides testing support for projects, system updates, and ongoing enhancements, including regression testing, impact analysis, and review of functional changes. Maintains and implements standards, documentation, security protocols, and best practices for Workday and other university applications. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong working knowledge of Workday architecture, business process framework, and security model (or equivalent enterprise/cloud ERP system, with willingness to develop deep Workday expertise). Ability to analyze complex business problems, identify root causes, and recommend practical, scalable solutions. Skill in gathering and documenting business requirements and translating them into system configuration and functional specifications. Ability to develop, execute, and evaluate detailed test plans and scripts. Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills; ability to interpret data and assess the downstream impact of configuration changes. Effective written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences. Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously, often with competing deadlines. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work collaboratively across functional teams, IT staff, and university stakeholders. Ability to train, mentor, and provide guidance to less-experienced analysts. Sound judgment and decision-making ability, particularly regarding system security, data integrity, and process design. High degree of discretion in handling confidential and sensitive institutional data. Proficiency with report writing and data query tools; familiarity with integration concepts (APIs, EIBs) preferred. Ability to adapt to evolving system functionality, including Workday's ongoing release cycle. Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, Business Administration, or related field; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum of 3-5 years of experience in business/systems analysis, with direct experience supporting an enterprise resource planning (ERP) or human capital management (HCM) system required; Workday experience strongly preferred. Experience with business process configuration, security administration, and/or report writing within a large enterprise system preferred. Higher education industry experience is a plus.  Prior experience supporting Human Resource is strongly preferred. Workday certification(s) in a relevant functional area (e.g., HCM, Financials, Integrations, Report Writer) preferred or may be required to obtain within a defined period after hire. ‌ Posted Salary: $58,500 ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Primarily sedentary work, requiring the ability to sit for extended periods at a computer workstation. Regular use of hands and fingers for typing, data entry, and use of a computer mouse. Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing, including via phone, email, and virtual meeting platforms. Ability to see and read computer screens and printed materials for extended periods. Occasional standing, walking, bending, or reaching to access files, equipment, or attend in-person meetings. Occasional lifting of up to 15-20 lbs (e.g., laptop, office equipment, training materials). Reasonable accommodations will be made for individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Professor-in-Psychological-Science--Open-Area-_JR100445": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Psychological Science (Open Area)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor in Psychological Science (Open Area) ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Department of Psychological Science at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Psychology beginning August 2027. Candidates should be strongly committed to teaching at the undergraduate level, engaging undergraduates in research, and applying rigorous scientific principles to the study of psychology. Area of specialization is open. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in clinical/counseling psychology, lifespan development, industrial/organizational psychology, or human factors. The department offers a collegial work environment that values both teaching and scholarship. Departmental scholarly interests span clinical, developmental, health, social, cognitive, and industrial/organizational psychology, along with neuroscience and psychopharmacology. More information about the department can be found on our website https://www.nku.edu/academics/artsci/about/departments/psychology/about.html. ‌ The Department of Psychological Science at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Psychology beginning August 2027. Candidates should be strongly committed to teaching at the undergraduate level, engaging undergraduates in research, and applying rigorous scientific principles to the study of psychology. Area of specialization is open. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in clinical/counseling psychology, lifespan development, industrial/organizational psychology, or human factors. The department offers a collegial work environment that values both teaching and scholarship. Departmental scholarly interests span clinical, developmental, health, social, cognitive, and industrial/organizational psychology, along with neuroscience and psychopharmacology. More information about the department can be found on our website https://www.nku.edu/academics/artsci/about/departments/psychology/about.html .   Northern Kentucky University (NKU) is a public, comprehensive university of approximately 15,000 students supported by more than 2,000 faculty and staff. Located on a vibrant suburban campus in Highland Heights—just seven miles southeast of downtown Cincinnati—we deliver innovative, learner‑centered education and conduct impactful scholarship that prepares students for rewarding careers while strengthening the region’s social and economic vitality.  NKU’s vision is that we will be nationally recognized for being a student-ready, regionally engaged university that empowers diverse learners for economic and social mobility. Our core values place emphasis on our culture of excellence, creativity, innovation, and collegiality.  Our strategic framework emphasizes (1) expanding and enhancing student access, success, and career readiness, (2) creating a supportive and sustainable work environment to attract and retain talent, and (3) advancing economic, social, and civic vitality in our community and region. The University provides equal opportunities in educational services and employment according to the law.   Primary Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach undergraduate in-person classes, as well as courses offered for our online BA program. In-person and online courses will include Introduction to Psychology, Research Methods and Lab, and courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise.  The successful candidate will also maintain an active, peer-reviewed research agenda consistent with the department’s emphasis on scientific rigor.   Qualifications A Ph.D. in psychology from a regionally or nationally accredited university by August 1, 2027, is required.   Candidates should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement, research statement including a plan for incorporating undergraduate students, up to three reprints/preprints, and names and email addresses of three references. Candidates with teaching experience should also submit evidence of teaching proficiency (e.g., teaching evaluations, example syllabi, etc.). The cover letter and teaching statement should show, as a faculty member at NKU, how the candidate will contribute to our core values and our strategic framework, especially in how the candidate will contribute to student success and belonging.  Application materials should be submitted electronically to  https://jobs.nku.edu/ . Once an application has been processed, a secure link will be sent to the three reference providers so that letters of recommendation can be uploaded to the same website. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be directed to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Kim Breitenbecher (breitenbeche@nku.edu, 859-572-5519). ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Part-time-Instructor_JR100452": {
      "title": "Part time Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Part time Instructor ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Department of Sociology, Anthropology and Philosophy invites applications for a part-time Adjunct Instructor in anthropology, sociology, philosophy, and religious studies. ‌ Candidates will teach one or more of the following classes: Introduction to cultural anthropology; Introduction to archaeology (prehistory); World cultures; Introduction to sociology; Sociology of global inequalities; Philosophy, individuals, and society; Introduction to logic; Philosophers, cultures, and creativity, Philosophy of ethics; Information ethics Health care ethics; World religions and cultures. Courses may be offered on NKU’s campus, online, or at area high schools. For additional information on the department visit http://nku.edu/sap. M.A. in anthropology, sociology, philosophy, or religious studies required. Please submit your application with a cover letter, vitae, and the names of at least three professional references. Completed applications will be kept on file for future opportunities. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Two-Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-Positions-in-Information-Systems---Analytics_JR100430": {
      "title": "Two Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Positions in Information Systems & Analytics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Two Tenure-Track Assistant Professor Positions in Information Systems & Analytics ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Assistant Professors in Information Systems and Analytics ‌ The School of Computing and Analytics (SCA) at Northern Kentucky University (NKU) invites applications for two full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Information Systems and Analytics beginning August 2027. Salary and benefits are competitive. We are seeking candidates possessing teaching and/or research expertise in one or more of the following areas: information systems, security management, analytics and data-driven decision-making, health informatics, health information systems, health information management, or artificial intelligence in healthcare. The positions will contribute to the Information Systems & Analytics (IS&A) programs: B.S. in Information Systems and Business Informatics, M.S. in Information Systems, and M.S. in Health Informatics. Learn more about the IS&A programs at https://www.nku.edu/informatics/schools/sca/programs/isa/index.html . The SCA is part of the College of Informatics (COI) (informatics.nku.edu) and is housed in Griffin Hall, a landmark high-tech building. The School offers multiple degrees and is organized into three program clusters: Computer Science & Software Engineering (CS&SE), Cybersecurity & Information Technology (CYS&IT), and Information Systems & Analytics (IS&A). More information about the SCA is available at https://www.nku.edu/informatics/schools/sca/index.html . Teaching: Develop and teach both face-to-face and online courses. The standard teaching load in the Information Systems & Analytics program is three courses per semester for active researchers. The candidate will be expected to teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Research: Maintain an active research agenda in the field to ensure ongoing qualification as a Scholarly Academic (SA) under AACSB accreditation standards. Service: Participate in service activities, including serving on committees at the School, College, and University levels and/or contributing to the professional community. On-campus presence: This is not a remote position . The successful candidates will be required to relocate to the Northern Kentucky/Greater Cincinnati area. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Information Systems or a closely related field preferably from an AACSB-accredited program. ABD candidates will be considered. Documents should be submitted as part of the application process. Must apply on the NKU Jobs website at: https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External Please upload the following (all documents can be submitted in the same documents box): Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching interests (required for all applicants) Statement of research interests (required for tenure-track applicants) List of three references with complete contact information Priority will be given to applications received by November 1, 2026 . Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Questions concerning this position should be addressed to: Mahathi Koutha, koutham1@nku.edu , 859-572-5240 All offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law. NKU’s vision is that we will be nationally recognized for being a student-ready, regionally engaged university that empowers diverse learners for economic and social mobility. Our core values place emphasis on our culture of excellence, creativity, innovation, and collegiality. Your cover letter and/or teaching statement should show, as a faculty member at NKU, how you will contribute to our core values and our strategic framework, especially in how you will contribute to student success and belonging. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Professor-of-Construction-Management-Construction_JR100426": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management Construction",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Construction Management Construction ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Construction Management program in the Haile College of Business at Northern Kentucky University seeks applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level to begin in Fall 2027. We invite candidates from all areas of specialization to apply; particular consideration will be given to those with expertise in: Construction Materials, Construction layout and surveying, construction safety, construction equipment, Project Costing and Cost Control, Sustainable Construction, Virtual Construction, and Smart Buildings, and heavy/civil construction. ‌ Salary will be based on a nine-month, academic year appointment. The Construction Management program is housed in the multidisciplinary department of Marketing, Sports Business & Event Management, and Construction Management. Currently, the program has approximately 160 undergraduate students and 4 full time faculty.The program enjoys the support of key construction firms in the tri-state area represented on its active industry advisory board. The AACSB- and ACCE-accredited Haile College of Business serves over 2,800 of NKU’s 14,000+ students with a full complement of traditional degree programs, plus several nationally recognized institutes, centers, and specialized programs. We are proud to offer an outstanding comprehensive university environment to faculty who value a well-rounded career path of high-quality student interaction, productive, meaningful research, and rewarding civic engagement. Located seven miles from downtown Cincinnati in an area offering an outstanding quality of life, NKU is a nationally recognized metropolitan university committed to active engagement with the Northern Kentucky/Greater Cincinnati region of nearly two million people. Additional information may be found on the college website athttp://cob.nku.edu. Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. To apply for this position, visit https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External?jobFamilyGroup=c6378c2d116f10006f42ee2cadfb0000 to submit a letter of interest, current curriculum vita, contact information for three references, statement of teaching philosophy, and statement of research goals. Questions should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Ihab Saad, at saadi1@nku.edu. Primary Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses; pursue scholarship of teaching, research, and/or outreach in accordance with the mission of the university; fully participate in the assessment of student learning outcomes; work with student organizations and/or mentor student competition teams; collaborate with other disciplines and interact with the industry; participate in service activity in support of the university and college missions; and participate in or lead service learning projects. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Certified-Personal-Trainer--Temp-Staff-_JR100461": {
      "title": "Certified Personal Trainer (Temp Staff)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Certified Personal Trainer (Temp Staff) ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: This position provides personal training services to NKU Campus Recreation members by leading individualized workouts and helping clients work toward their fitness goals. Personal Trainers will create and lead safe, effective exercise sessions while providing a welcoming and supportive experience for clients. ‌ Primary Responsibilities : Lead individualized personal training sessions for Campus Recreation members Develop safe and effective workouts based on clients’ goals and fitness levels Demonstrate proper exercise technique and provide coaching throughout sessions Modify exercises to meet individual client needs and abilities Track client workouts, progress, and session attendance Communicate with clients to schedule sessions and provide ongoing support Maintain a professional, welcoming, and clean training environment Minimum expectations for consideration: Current personal training certification from a nationally recognized organization Strong communication and interpersonal skills Ability to work independently and reliably Basic knowledge of exercise technique, fitness programming, and safety Ability to provide a welcoming and supportive experience for clients   Work Schedule and Pay: $15/hour Approximately 5–10 hours per week, depending on client demand and availability Schedule is flexible and will be coordinated around the trainer’s availability and client schedules Some early morning, evening, or weekend hours may be available/required based on client needs Documents to include in application: (Can be added in the same documents box) Resume outlining relevant education, experience, and certifications Copy of current personal training certification ‌ Posted Salary: $15/Hour ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Fitness-Instructor--Temp-Staff-_JR100462": {
      "title": "Fitness Instructor (Temp Staff)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-25\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Fitness Instructor (Temp Staff) ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: The Fitness Instructor leads safe and effective fitness classes, promotes proper exercise techniques, and creates a positive experience for participants. Instructors are expected to maintain clear communication, attend required trainings and meetings, and assist with cleaning and facility maintenance. ‌ Primary Responsibilities : Properly and safely instruct group fitness formats to participants. This includes accident prevention, proper techniques and guidelines. Other responsibilities include punctual attendance to all mandatory staff meetings, in-service trainings, and assistance with cleaning duties. Clear communication between employee(s) and employer is a must.   Qualifications : General: Ability to follow written and verbal directions, can commit to at least two semesters of teaching class(es) and friendly and customer service oriented. Skill: Obtain and maintain CPR/AED, and First Aid and national fitness certification such as AFAA, ACE, ACSM or Zumba or completion of in-house Group Fitness Instructor Training. Physical: To maintain fitness level required to be a group fitness instructor, attend and perform successfully at in-service training sessions.   Work Schedule : 25 hours per week $8.50/hr ‌ Posted Salary: $8.50/Hour ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Adjunct-Faculty-Pool--Master-of-Science-in-Health-Administration--MSHA-_JR100474": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool, Master of Science in Health Administration (MSHA)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct Faculty Pool, Master of Science in Health Administration (MSHA) ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University’s School of Allied Health is seeking applications for an adjunct faculty member to join the online accelerated Master of Science in Health Administration Program. The School of Allied Health, housed within the College of Health and Human Services, is a multidisciplinary unit offering both graduate and undergraduate clinical and non-clinical degree programs. Adjunct faculty members work under the leadership of MSHA full-time faculty members. Courses are designed by full-time faculty members according to NKU policies and standards. Adjunct faculty members assist full-time faculty members in presenting the course content assigned. Courses are delivered in seven-week online sessions using Canvas. Faculty are expected to maintain regular instructor presence, respond to student inquiries within 24-48 hours, provide substantive feedback on assignments, and submit final grades according to university deadlines. ‌ THERE IS NOT A SPECIFIC POSITION ASSOCIATED WITH THIS POSTING. THIS POSTING WILL BE USED TO CREATE A DATABASE OF POTENTIAL ADJUNCT FACULTY. Primary Responsibilities : Teach assigned courses as specified in the schedule and course contract fully online through NKU’s learning platform. Complete mandatory training for online instruction. Teach assigned courses in accordance with the approved syllabus, learning objectives, and instructional plan. Observe and evaluate student performance in meeting course objectives and learning outcomes through assignments, projects, discussions, and/or exams. Administer evaluations of student performance based on course deliverables and course rubrics. Provide feedback on student progress in a timely manner. Foster a supportive learning environment that encourages meaningful student engagement, respectful discussion, and academic success. Support student learning through regular communication, substantive feedback, and timely responses to student inquiries. Be available for student consultation. Maintain accurate and timely student records and grades within university systems Adhere to all expectations and policies as outlined in the provided NKU Faculty Handbook sections and applicable NKU policies. Qualifications : All adjuncts complete all program online instruction orientation(s) and training(s) regardless of previous online instruction experience or training. Candidates must have reliable high-speed internet, a webcam, microphone, and a computer capable of supporting current versions of web conferencing and learning management software. Earned doctoral degree (PhD, JD, MD, DHSc, DHA, etc.) in health administration/management, health policy, health law or related discipline. Demonstrated expertise through education and professional experience sufficient to teach graduate healthcare administration coursework. At least 5 years of experience as a leader/administrator in the healthcare industry. Skills and Knowledge Preferred : Prior teaching experience in a graduate or undergraduate program or corporate training Ability to use technology effectively in teaching Professional certifications such as FACHE, PMP, Lean Six Sigma, CPHQ, CHFP, etc. Experience in healthcare executive leadership. Please include: Cover letter that addresses the applicant's qualifications based on the position announcement. CV Contact information for three professional references Provide official transcripts to NKU Provost office Other : Complete any mandatory Online Faculty Orientation course(s) Any candidate who is offered this position will be required to go through a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Online program only"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Adjunct-Faculty---Counseling_JR100484": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct Faculty – Counseling ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Counseling Program at Northern Kentucky University invites applications on an ongoing basis from qualified professionals interested in serving as part-time adjunct faculty. Applications will be maintained in a pool of prospective instructors and reviewed as instructional needs arise. Inclusion in the applicant pool does not guarantee a teaching assignment. The Counseling Program offers CACREP-accredited graduate programs/specializations in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling. Adjunct faculty may be considered to teach in-person graduate courses in either specialization, including knowledge- and skills-based courses as well as courses involving clinical supervision, such as practicum and internship. Course assignments are based on program needs, candidate qualifications, areas of expertise, and availability. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Adjunct faculty are expected to: Teach assigned graduate counseling courses in accordance with university and program policies and applicable CACREP accreditation standards. Facilitate student learning through effective instruction, engagement, feedback, and assessment. Assess student achievement of designated course and CACREP learning outcomes. Maintain appropriate communication with students and program faculty. Provide in-person office hours and be reasonable availability to enrolled students. For clinical courses, provide supervision and evaluate student development in accordance with program requirements, professional standards, and applicable accreditation requirements. Complete required course-related documentation and assessment activities within established program and university timelines.   Minimum Qualifications Candidates must possess: A master’s degree or higher in counseling, preferably from a CACREP-accredited counseling program. Appropriate professional licensure or certification relevant to the candidate’s area of practice (e.g., clinical mental health counseling or school counseling). Professional experience relevant to the courses the candidate may be assigned to teach. Demonstrated ability to support graduate-level student learning and professional development. Candidates considered for courses involving clinical supervision must meet applicable program, professional, and CACREP requirements for supervisors.   Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to candidates who possess one or more of the following: A doctoral degree in Counselor Education and Supervision, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Previous experience teaching or co-teaching graduate counseling courses, particularly within a CACREP-accredited program. Experience providing clinical supervision to counseling students or practicing counselors. Current professional licensure or certification as a clinical mental health counselor, school counselor, or other credential appropriate to the assigned course. Professional expertise aligned with current program instructional needs.   Required Application Materials Applicants should submit: Curriculum vitae or résumé. Cover letter describing relevant teaching, counseling, and/or supervision experience and areas of instructional expertise. Sample syllabi from graduate courses previously taught or co-taught, if applicable. Evidence of current professional licensure and/or certification. Contact information for three professional references. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Applications will be reviewed as instructional needs arise. Candidates whose qualifications align with available courses may be contacted by the Counseling Program for additional information or an interview. Appointment to the adjunct faculty pool does not guarantee a course assignment. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Adjunct-Instructor--Exercise-Science_JR100483": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Exercise Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct Instructor, Exercise Science ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Exercise Science Program is seeking qualified adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate courses within the Exercise Science curriculum. Adjunct faculty contribute to the academic and professional preparation of students pursuing careers and graduate education in exercise science, fitness and wellness, strength and conditioning, allied health, and related fields. ‌ Responsibilities may include: • Teach one or more undergraduate Exercise Science courses based on program needs and the instructor's area of expertise. • Deliver high-quality, student-centered instruction in classroom, laboratory, virtually, and/or applied learning environments. • Prepare and deliver course content consistent with established course objectives, program learning outcomes, and departmental expectations. • Facilitate laboratory and experiential learning activities, when applicable, and provide appropriate instruction in the safe and effective use of exercise science equipment. • Assess student learning through appropriate assignments, examinations, practical assessments, and other evaluation methods. • Provide timely, constructive feedback to students and maintain accurate course and grade records. • Maintain appropriate availability for student questions, academic support, and mentoring related to the course. • Utilize the University's learning management system and other instructional technologies to support student learning and course administration. • Collaborate with Exercise Science faculty and program leadership to promote consistency, academic quality, and student success across the curriculum. • Incorporate current evidence, professional standards, and relevant real-world applications into course instruction. • Complete required University and departmental training and fulfill administrative responsibilities associated with the assigned course(s). Minimum Qualifications • Master's degree in Exercise Science, Exercise Physiology, Kinesiology, Human Performance, Biomechanics, Strength and Conditioning, Athletic Training, or another closely related field from an accredited institution. • Graduate-level academic preparation and/or professional expertise appropriate to the course(s) assigned. • Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with undergraduate students. • Ability to effectively organize and deliver course content and assess student learning. • Ability to work collaboratively and professionally with students, faculty, staff, and program leadership. • Ability to use or learn instructional technologies and learning management systems required for course delivery. Preferred Qualifications • Doctoral degree or doctoral coursework in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Exercise Physiology, Human Performance, or a closely related discipline. • Previous experience teaching Exercise Science, Kinesiology, or related courses at the college or university level. • Professional experience in exercise science, fitness, wellness, clinical exercise physiology, strength and conditioning, sport performance, or a related setting. • Experience teaching laboratory-based or experiential courses, including familiarity with exercise testing, fitness assessment, and/or human performance laboratory equipment. • Current professional certification relevant to the individual's area of expertise, such as ACSM, NSCA, or another nationally recognized credential. • Experience teaching courses in one or more areas of the Exercise Science curriculum, such as exercise physiology, exercise testing and prescription, strength and conditioning, biomechanics/kinesiology, sport and exercise psychology, fitness and wellness, research methods, or related areas. • Experience integrating current research and evidence-based professional practice into undergraduate instruction. Preferred Skills • Strong teaching, presentation, and interpersonal communication skills. • Ability to engage students with varied academic backgrounds, career goals, and levels of experience. • Ability to translate scientific concepts into practical applications relevant to exercise science and allied health careers. • Commitment to active, experiential, and student-centered learning. • Strong organizational and time-management skills, including the ability to provide timely feedback and meet academic deadlines. • Ability to foster a supportive, professional, and academically rigorous learning environment. • Effective collaboration and communication with full-time faculty, adjunct colleagues, and program leadership. • Familiarity with contemporary technologies used in exercise science education and professional practice. • Commitment to remaining current with developments, professional standards, and evidence-based practices within the field. Please provide CV/resume and cover letter ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Adjunct-CRNA-Simulation---Clinical-Education-Faculty_JR100482": {
      "title": "Adjunct CRNA Simulation & Clinical Education Faculty",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Adjunct CRNA Simulation & Clinical Education Faculty ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Northern Kentucky University Nurse Anesthesia Program is seeking an experienced Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA) to support the education and professional development of nurse anesthesia students through didactic instruction, lecture-based teaching, simulation, and hands-on clinical skills training. Working collaboratively with Nurse Anesthesia Program faculty, the CRNA educator will provide classroom instruction in areas of clinical expertise, facilitate simulation-based learning, and assist with skills laboratory experiences. The position will help students connect foundational and advanced anesthesia concepts with clinical practice through evidence-based instruction, case discussion, simulation, demonstration, and guided practice. The CRNA educator will contribute to a student-centered learning environment that promotes clinical reasoning, critical thinking, technical proficiency, professionalism, and progressive development toward safe and competent nurse anesthesia practice. This role provides an opportunity for a practicing CRNA to bring current, real-world anesthesia experience into both the classroom and simulation environment. ‌ Requirements/Qualifications Current certification/recertification as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA) through the NBCRNA Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse license Current license/privilege to practice as an APRN/CRNA in accordance with applicable state law Graduate degree in nurse anesthesia; master's or doctoral preparation preferred/required as appropriate for faculty appointment Current clinical practice and demonstrated clinical competency Commitment to maintaining professional development and evidence-based anesthesia practice Ability to effectively teach, demonstrate clinical skills, provide feedback, and serve as a professional role model Strong communication, interpersonal, and collaborative skills Ability to promote critical thinking, clinical judgment, student independence, and progressive development Commitment to professional standards, ethical practice, and the mission and goals of the NKU Nurse Anesthesia Program Responsibilities/Duties The CRNA educator will collaborate with NKU Nurse Anesthesia Program faculty to provide simulation, skills laboratory, and other educational experiences for nurse anesthesia students. Responsibilities may include: The CRNA educator will collaborate with Nurse Anesthesia Program faculty to provide didactic, simulation-based, and experiential instruction throughout the nurse anesthesia curriculum. Responsibilities may include: Prepare and deliver classroom lectures and presentations on anesthesia-related topics within the CRNA's areas of clinical expertise. Translate current clinical practice and evidence-based anesthesia principles into meaningful, clinically relevant classroom instruction. Facilitate case-based discussions, clinical correlation activities, and other interactive learning experiences that help students integrate didactic knowledge with anesthesia practice. Facilitate and assist with high-fidelity simulation, task training, skills laboratories, workshops, and other experiential learning activities. Teach and demonstrate anesthesia-related technical and psychomotor skills, including airway management, anesthesia equipment, patient assessment, anesthetic planning, monitoring, and other skills appropriate to the student's level of progression. Participate in simulation prebriefing, scenario facilitation, debriefing, and student evaluation. Create an educational environment that encourages active learning, inquiry, clinical reasoning, critical thinking, and problem-solving. Demonstrate expert anesthesia practice and serve as a professional role model for students. Provide timely and constructive feedback regarding student knowledge, clinical reasoning, technical performance, communication, and professionalism. Assist program faculty with the development, implementation, and evaluation of lectures, simulation scenarios, skills-training activities, and other instructional materials. Participate in student assessment and remediation activities as requested by program faculty. Incorporate current evidence, professional standards, and contemporary anesthesia practice into teaching activities. Collaborate with program faculty to ensure educational activities support course objectives, student learning outcomes, and progressive development throughout the curriculum. Assist with preparation, organization, and appropriate use of simulation equipment and learning spaces. Maintain professional and ethical standards and comply with applicable NKU, College of Health and Human Services, School of Nursing, and Nurse Anesthesia Program policies. Required Documents Curriculum Vitae (CV) or résumé Copy of current NBCRNA certification/recertification Documentation of current RN and APRN/CRNA licensure Official graduate transcript(s) ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-in-Physics_JR100453": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure Track Assistant Professor in Physics ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Department of Physics, Geology, and Engineering Technology (PGET) at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor in all areas of Experimental Physics or Engineering Physics to begin August 2027. We will consider candidates who have achieved ABD status. ‌ Required Qualifications : A doctorate degree in Physics, or related field is required by the time of the appointment (August 2027) Expertise in experimental physics or engineering physics. Ability to establish a research program in physics or engineering physics that involves undergraduate student researchers. Proven record of scholarly research in physics or engineering physics. Ability to teach physics courses both at the introductory and upper levels   Preferred Qualifications :   Experience in teaching undergraduate-level courses effectively. Ability to mentor capstone projects Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students with diverse social identities and backgrounds Responsibilities : Core responsibilities for this job includes, but not limited to: Teach physics courses,  both introductory and upper level Establish an active and sustainable research program that involves NKU’s undergraduate students Support  the engineering physics  and  the pre-engineering programs Promote student engagement and improve the quality of undergraduate learning Participate in service activities of the department The PGET department has 10 tenured/tenure-track faculty members and 4 full-time, non-tenured faculty who serve approximately 260 students enrolled in its programs. The department, will be housed in the newly renovated Herrmann Science Center and its expansion, which is due to be completed in Spring 2027. The department offers baccalaureate degrees in physics, engineering physics, geology, and three specialties in engineering technology as well as pre-engineering transfer programs. More information about the department can be found in the web page, https://www.nku.edu/artsci/departments/pget/index.html The  department offers a BS degree in Engineering Physics: it has four tracks and  consists of courses in physics and engineering technology. The pre-engineering program is geared for students who plans to transfer to engineering programs after two or three years at NKU. The program also offers a BA and a BS in physics: The BA is suitable for a dual major with a second major in engineering physics, mathematics or education. The BS is suitable for a student who wants to pursue a graduate degree in physics.. There are  approximately  60 undergraduate Physics majors, Engineering Physics majors  and pre-engineering students currently. The department provides ample opportunities for undergraduate research in physics. For more information on the Physics and Engineering Physics Programs at NKU please visit: https://www.nku.edu/academics/programs/index.html#/results?keyword=Department+of+Physics,+Geology,+%26+Engineering+Technology&interests=&types= College of Arts and Sciences and the Department actively support new faculty with professional development and mentoring opportunities: these includes but not limited to, start-up support for research, internal grants for research, funds for conference travel and stipends for research students. NKU also offers faculty development grants which are supported via the Provost’s office including summer fellowships, projects grants and sabbatical leave for tenured faculty every six years. Teaching load in the College of Arts and Sciences is usually 12 credit hours a week. In the Engineering Physics and Physics programs this spans the entire undergraduate physics curriculum, which includes introductory and advanced courses for majors, general education courses and lab courses. NKU is a comprehensive regional university of approximately 15,000 students located seven miles from downtown Cincinnati, OH in an area offering an outstanding quality of life. It is near a variety of natural areas and is a nationally recognized metropolitan university committed to active engagement with the Northern Kentucky/Greater Cincinnati region of nearly two million people. The university has been recognized as one of America’s most military-friendly and disability-friendly schools. NKU’s vision is that we will be nationally recognized for being a student-ready, regionally engaged university that empowers diverse learners for economic and social mobility. Our core values place emphasis on our culture of excellence, creativity, innovation, and collegiality . For additional information on NKU visit https://www.nku.edu/ Candidates should submit: a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy, a statement of research plan, and email and phone numbers of at least three references. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Sharmanthie Fernando ( fernando@nku.edu ) for any questions. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Professor-of-Scenic-Design_JR100490": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Scenic Design",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Professor of Scenic Design ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Theatre & Dance Program is seeking an active, professional artist to join our collaborative, diverse, and vibrant program located in the artistically rich greater Cincinnati area. The School of the Arts at Northern Kentucky University offers a wide array of degree programs in the visual and performing arts. The Theatre & Dance Program within the School of the Arts offers a BFA in Theatre Performance (with tracks in Acting, Musical Theatre, Dance Performance, Dance Pedagogy, and Playwriting), a BFA in Theatre Design, Technology, or Stage Management (with tracks in Theatre Design or Technology, and Stage Management), a BA in Theatre Arts, a Dance Minor, and a Theatre Minor. See the Theatre & Dance website at theatre.nku.edu for additional information. ‌ Primary responsibilities include teaching design courses for the program, designing scenery, projections (including control and mapping ), and/or props for mainstage season productions, scene painting , participating in production strikes , providing leadership and mentorship of students in the design area, recruiting and mentoring majors within the design area of the program, active participation/mentoring of students during scene shop lab, and shared oversight of paint/props/projection studio. Possible teaching responsibilities may include scenic design, projection design, control and mapping , properties design, scenic painting, drafting, Vectorworks, rendering, fundamentals of design, and special topics in design. Other duties will be assigned based on the candidate’s strengths, interests, and the needs of the program. Responsibilities also include the development of a scholarly/creative agenda in research, performance, and/or professional creative activities.  Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree (MFA) required Record of excellence in Scene Design with strengths in conceptual design, rendering and/or modeling, drafting and scenic painting. Candidate should also have a breadth of professional creative activity. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of potential for a successful career in teaching.  Working knowledge of projection design and control for theatre/ entertainment.  Experience cultivating positive and collaborative relationships in the industry and region. Ability to work effectively with students of varied backgrounds, abilities, and goals for access and opportunity. Strong organizational and communication skills to support the operation of a growing theatrical design and technology program.  Demonstrated success in recruiting and retaining students.  Ability to work collaboratively and cultivate a positive working environment with both students and colleagues. Candidates who have additional positive attributes/expertise/skills beyond the above qualifications are desirable and should reference these additional attributes in application materials. Application For primary consideration for this position, a complete application must be received by midnight on Friday, November 2 . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. Applications received after the deadline will only be considered if additional qualified candidates are sought. Selected candidates must successfully pass a background check. Applicants who enrich the diversity of the campus community are strongly encouraged to apply. Finalist candidates should expect to give a creative/scholarly portfolio presentation, teaching demonstration, and committee interview during an on-campus interview. Required materials to include:  (All materials can be submitted in the same documents box) A 1–2-page cover letter that describes how well the applicant satisfies the qualifications, experience, and teaching effectiveness needed for this position and how the applicant will specifically contribute to the success of the Theatre & Dance Program at NKU.  A Curriculum Vitae.  A 1-2-page statement of your personal philosophy regarding hands-on collaboration/mentorship in the production and design process and why they are important in higher education. Please also include specifics regarding your commitment and/or experience promoting and fostering a learning environment that is supportive of individuals from diverse backgrounds.  A one-page personal teaching philosophy statement reflecting your approach in the classroom.   A document with the names and contact information (phone and email) for at least three (3) professional references who can speak to your teaching, mentorship, and collaboration in the production process as well as leadership in their assigned areas of production.  A document with unrestricted links (please use online platforms such as YouTube, Vimeo, etc., and test all links to ensure they are working correctly) to your design portfolio.  Unofficial transcripts.  Questions   Questions regarding the use of this website should be directed to the Human Resources Department at hr@nku.edu. Questions regarding the nature of the position should be directed to the search committee chair, Michael Hatton, hattonm@nku.edu . Candidates should submit materials electronically at: Assistant Professor of Scenic Design .   ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Manager--EngageKY-Communications-and-Engagement_JR100460": {
      "title": "Manager, EngageKY Communications and Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Manager, EngageKY Communications and Engagement ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: EngageKY is seeking a creative, strategic, and relationship-driven Manager of Communications and Engagement to help tell our story, grow our impact, and strengthen our connections across Kentucky. This role brings together communications, marketing, events, program strategy, and stakeholder engagement to increase awareness of EngageKY’s work and create new opportunities for growth and partnership. The ideal candidate is both a big-picture thinker and a hands-on doer who can develop compelling stories and campaigns, create engaging digital and print content, lead high-quality events, build meaningful partnerships, and use data to understand what is working. If you enjoy turning great ideas into action and want to use your skills to support programs that strengthen communities across Kentucky, we’d love to hear from you. ‌ The Manager of Communications and Engagement provides strategic leadership for EngageKY’s communications, marketing, external engagement, events, and program advancement efforts. Working closely with the Executive Director and organizational leadership, the Manager helps translate EngageKY’s strategic priorities into initiatives that strengthen programs, expand partnerships, increase organizational visibility, and demonstrate impact. The position uses data, storytelling, relationship development, and strategic communications to advance EngageKY’s mission and support sustainable organizational growth. Communications and Marketing Leadership Develop and implement a comprehensive communications and marketing strategy aligned with EngageKY’s mission, programs, and growth priorities. Create integrated, multi-channel communications plans across web, email, social media, CRM, print, and other platforms. Translate organizational goals and program outcomes into compelling stories and measurable communications initiatives. Lead organizational messaging, storytelling, brand positioning, and content strategy. Manage content development and distribution across EngageKY’s digital platforms and public-facing communications. Oversee the development, design, and distribution of annual reports, impact reports, promotional materials, presentations, and other organizational collateral. Create print and digital materials, including brochures, booklets, handbooks, displays, programs, posters, social media graphics, web content, and email campaigns. Maintain EngageKY’s website content and coordinate updates and improvements as needed. Ensure consistent application of EngageKY’s brand identity, voice, logos, graphics, and messaging across organizational materials. Monitor communications and engagement analytics and use results to refine strategies and increase reach and effectiveness. Event Coordination Assist in the planning and execution of EngageKY external events from initial concept through implementation, evaluation, and follow-up. Develop event strategies, project plans, budgets, sponsorship models, timelines, staffing plans, and promotional strategies. Coordinate with program and operations staff on logistics, vendors, technology, registration, accessibility, and other event needs. Support the planning and promotion of training events and other program-related experiences as needed. Oversee event communications, marketing, sponsorship visibility, participant engagement, and post-event stewardship. Ensure events support EngageKY’s broader programmatic, advancement, partnership, and brand objectives. Develop appropriate risk management and contingency plans for major events. Coordinate virtual, hybrid, and in-person event experiences. Evaluate events using financial, participation, engagement, partnership, and relationship-based measures of success. Brand Awareness Coordinate organizational representation and messaging to ensure EngageKY presents a consistent and compelling public presence. Manage newsletter and social media channels to connect with stakeholders. Serve as a connector across programs to identify opportunities for shared communications, partnerships, events, and organizational storytelling. The Manager of Communications and Engagement performs other duties as assigned and contributes to a collaborative organizational culture focused on service, innovation, accountability, and measurable community impact. Pay Minimum $42, 549 Annually ‌ Posted Salary: Minimum $42,549 Annually ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Processing-Archivist_JR100465": {
      "title": "Processing Archivist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Processing Archivist ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Under the direction of the University Archivist (Head of Special Collections and University Archives) the Processing Archivist for Special Collections and University Archives is responsible for the accessioning, arrangement, description, preservation and accessibility of the university's archival and manuscript collections. This position supports both the University Archives and Special Collections by managing physical and digital collections, providing reference and instructional services, contributing to digital initiatives, collaborating with campus partners to preserve and promote the history of Northern Kentucky University and the surrounding region. The Archivist also assists in administering the University's Records and Information Management (RIM) Program by supporting records transfers, records stewardship, and outreach to university departments. In addition, the position supervises student employees and fellows, providing training, project oversight, and experiential learning opportunities that support departmental initiatives. Working closely with the Head of Special Collections & University Archives, this position contributes to strategic initiatives that expand access to collections, strengthen records stewardship, support teaching and learning, enhance digital stewardship, and increase campus and community engagement. ‌ Job Responsibilities: Collection Processing and Description Arrange and describe archival collections following archival standards including DACS and other applicable descriptive practices Create, edit, and maintain collection records and finding aids in ArchivesSpace. Process university records, manuscripts, photographs, audiovisual materials, and born-digital collections. Conduct preservation assessments and recommend appropriate rehousing and conservation measures. Manage accessioning workflows and documentation. University Archives and Records Stewardship Coordinate the acquisition and transfer of university records documenting the history and operations of Northern Kentucky University. Maintain documentation related to university archival collections and records transfers and destructions. Assist in implementing and supporting university records management initiatives. Collaborate with university departments to identify records of enduring historical value. Digital Collections and Archives Assist with digitization initiatives and digital preservation workflows. Contribute to digital exhibits and online access initiatives Support quality control for digitized materials and associated metadata Student Employee Supervision Responsible for hiring, training, scheduling, supervising, and evaluating 1-3 student employees supporting the work of Special Collections &University Archives. Trains student employees in archival processing procedures and standards, including arrangement and description, collection handling, rehousing and preservation practices, inventory creation, metadata entry, and the use of archival collection management systems. Assigns and monitors student processing projects, provides ongoing guidance and feedback, and reviews completed work to ensure accuracy, consistency, and adherence to departmental standards and professional archival practices. Provides students with opportunities to develop practical experience in archival work while ensuring that assigned projects support SCUA's processing, preservation, and access priorities. Outreach and Public Engagement Assist with exhibits, public programming, and outreach initiatives highlighting SCUA collections. Collaborate with library colleagues on instructional workshops and campus engagement activities. Promote awareness and use of archival collections through presentations and events. Contribute content for library communications and digital platforms. Assist with reference services for students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external researchers, including helping researchers in locating and interpreting archival resources. Assessmen t Participate in maintaining statistics related to collections, instruction, and reference services/public access. Contributes to departmental planning, projects, and initiatives that support the mission and strategic priorities of SCUA and Steely Library. Other Duties as Assigned. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS & ABILITIES: Excellent analytical, research, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to evaluate information, synthesize findings, and apply sound professional judgment. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and public speaking skills, with the ability to provide instruction, deliver presentations, and communicate effectively with diverse audiences. Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to exercise sound professional judgment when appraising, processing, describing, preserving, and providing access to archival materials. Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects, establish priorities, and meet deadlines. Demonstrated ability to work independently while contributing effectively as a collaborative member of a team. Knowledge of archival theory and practice, including archival processing, arrangement, description, preservation, and access. Knowledge of Records and Information Management (RIM) principles, best practices, applicable legal requirements, and Kentucky State Records Laws. Comprehensive knowledge of university organizational structure, governance, and administrative functions, or the ability to quickly develop such knowledge. Demonstrated knowledge of digital preservation theory, standards, technologies, and best practices. Experience creating standards-compliant metadata for digital repositories, archival collection management systems, or digital asset management systems. Experience with archival collection management systems (e.g., ArchivesSpace), digital repositories, metadata standards, and data import/export or migration processes. Ability to learn and effectively utilize archival, records management, digitization, and digital collections technologies. Strong commitment to access, stewardship, and inclusive archival description. Ability to supervise, train, and mentor student employees, fellows, interns, and volunteers. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, donors, alumni, researchers, and community partners. Ability to balance stewardship responsibilities with providing broad access to archival and special collections materials in support of teaching, learning, research, and community engagement. Commitment to providing excellent public service and fostering a welcoming research environment. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: Required Qualifications Master's degree in Library and Information Science (MUS), Public History, Archival Studies, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Five (5) years of progressively responsible professional experience in archives, special collections, records management, or a related field. Equivalent combinations of education and experience may be considered. A bachelor's degree in a related field with a minimum of eight (8) years of progressively responsible, directly applicable experience may be substituted for the master's degree. Coursework in archives, archival administration, records management, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated knowledge of archival theory, principles, and best practices, including records lifecycle management, appraisal, accessioning, arrangement and description, preservation, and access. Knowledge of records management principles, including records lifecycle concepts, retention schedules, legal and regulatory compliance, records appraisal, and information governance. Experience processing archival and manuscript collections using current professional standards, including DACS, EAD, controlled vocabularies, and archival collection management systems such as ArchivesSpace. Demonstrated ability to organize, prioritize, and manage multiple projects while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, donors, and community partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience with digital preservation, born-digital records, digitization workflows, and archival technologies, including archival content management systems, digital asset management systems, digital repositories, and discovery platforms such as ArchivesSpace, Preservica, DSpace, Omeka, or similar systems. Experience working in an academic library, university archives, special collections, or cultural heritage institution. Experience supervising, mentoring, or training student employees, interns, graduate assistants, or volunteers. Pay Minimum $42,549 Annually ‌ Posted Salary: Minimum $42,549 Annually ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-of-Philosophy_JR100473": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy in the Department of Sociology, Anthropology, and Philosophy, beginning August 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to NKU's mission of delivering innovative, student-centered education and will support the Philosophy program's commitment to critical thinking, ethical reasoning, civic engagement, and student success. This position combines excellence in undergraduate teaching with leadership of an ethics center dedicated to ethical inquiry, public engagement, interdisciplinary collaboration, and community partnership. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Teaching and Student Success : Teach undergraduate philosophy courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats; advise and mentor students; participate in assessment, curriculum development, recruitment, retention, and co-curricular programming. Center Leadership and Community Engagement : Provide strategic leadership for the Center for Applied Ethics; develop partnerships with community organizations, businesses, healthcare institutions, schools, and government agencies; organize lectures, workshops, forums, and public programs; foster experiential learning opportunities; pursue grants and external funding; and represent NKU in regional and national conversations on ethics and civic responsibility. The Director will be expected to develop a sustainable revenue model for the Center through grants, gifts, sponsorships, and community partnerships.   Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Philosophy or a closely related field by the start date. Demonstrated commitment to effective undergraduate teaching and student success.   Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Philosophy. Evidence of successful college-level teaching. Experience teaching ethics and applied philosophy courses, including Philosophy and AI, Philosophy of Technology, Information Ethics, Professional Ethics, or related areas. Experience with community engagement, partnership development, center leadership, grant activity, public programming, or applied ethics initiatives.   About NKU Northern Kentucky University is a student-ready, regionally engaged university committed to transforming lives through innovative, student-centered education and impactful scholarly and creative work. NKU prepares graduates for fulfilling careers, meaningful lives, and active contributions to the economic, civic, and social well-being of the region. The university seeks faculty who contribute to excellence, collegiality, student success, engagement, and belonging.   Application Materials (all can be uploaded to the same documents box) Cover letter addressing qualifications for both the faculty position and Center directorship. Curriculum vitae. Teaching philosophy statement. Applied Ethics Leadership Statement (2–3 pages) describing the candidate’s vision for the Center, including outreach, partnerships, public programming, experiential learning, external engagement, external grant application/fund-raising. Statement describing contributions to NKU’s mission, values, student success, and belonging. Unofficial graduate transcripts. Contact information for three professional references.   Application Process Applications must be submitted through NKU Workday. Review of applications will begin on October 30, 2026 , and will continue until the position is filled. For full consideration, all application materials should be submitted by this date. Inquiries about the position may be directed to the Department Chair at frimpongma1@nku.edu .   Equal Opportunity Statement Northern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access/Affirmative Action institution and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Registrar--Systems_JR100476": {
      "title": "Assistant Registrar, Systems",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Registrar, Systems ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Registrar of Systems furthers the focus on student support as the position supervises the SIS, maintains program and course curriculum in SAP, manages the undergraduate catalog production and maintenance, manages the Registrar records room and creates and maintains the student records retention schedule.  Supervises Document Imaging and Curriculum Coordinator and Catalog Coordinator.  Manages course scheduling, system testing, data quality and degree audits ‌ Duties/Responsibilities Curriculum Maintenance: Maintains and updates the University's undergraduate and graduate curriculum in SAP to ensure that classes can be scheduled, students can register for them, and courses can be reported correctly.  Interprets curriculum policies and makes decisions on each curriculum form for input in the SAP system.  Works in conjunction with the University Curriculum Committee Chair and Curriculum, Accreditation and Assessment to make decisions regarding course curriculum and policies as well as solutions to issues regarding curriculum.  Answers questions from faculty and staff across all departments regarding course curriculum and policy interpretation.  Represents the Office of the University Registrar at Curriculum Committee and Graduate Council meetings. Catalog Creation and Maintenance:  Oversees the undergraduate catalog production and maintenance, responsible for updates in all Registrar owned catalog copy in catalog software.  Responsible for working with colleagues in the office and obtaining yearly updates on all policies and input into catalog software. Collaborates with IT to ensure course functionality including pre and co-requisites as well as run periodic reports.  Reviews annual upload of all course descriptions to catalog software and compares approved course descriptions to academic unit listings to ensure only approved curriculum is populated for undergraduate and graduate catalogs. Supervises the University's catalog coordinator to ensure proper transfer of information to the catalog as well as University editor to comply with University style guide. Supervision:  Trains, supervises and evaluates the job performance of the Document Imaging and Curriculum Coordinator and Catalog/Curriculum Coordinator, Systems Coordinator, and Course Scheduling Coordinator.  Conducts regular staff meetings, ensures staff have appropriate access and on-going training and works with individual staff members to develop professional development goals.     Records Retention:  Oversees the organization and maintenance of the records room in the Office of the University Registrar.  Responsible for ensuring the security and preservation of confidential student records.  Works with the University Archivist and Document Imaging Coordinator to create and implement the records retention schedule in compliance with federal privacy regulations (FERPA), AACRAO guidelines and state laws.  Works closely with University IT staff to remain informed about new technology available to enhance imaging system and processes. Oversees system updates and maintenance for the academic calendar, academic structure, advising holds, booking windows, and degree audit.  Maintains departmental computer inventory lists.  Ad hoc reporting/data requests/military data (in conjunction with compliance). Grading, final, and midterm. NSCH – core file, degree file and student tracker. POP forms (project opportunity proposal). Removing a change lock. SLCM security processing. System configuration. System maintenance. System testing (in conjunction with functional staff). Office master process calendar. Workflow set-up and maintenance. Responsible for data quality audits and troubleshooting. Responsible for end of semester grades, progression and academic standing. Helps support various specialized software (e.g. Ad Astra, catalog, Diplomas on Demand, Phone Tree). Oversee course and room scheduling process. Performs additional duties as might be required or assigned by Registrar leadership. Bachelor's and 3 years' related experience required. Minimum Salary of $42,549 Annually ‌ Posted Salary: $42,549 Minimum Annually ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--MSN-PMHNP-track_JR100486": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, MSN PMHNP track",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor, MSN PMHNP track ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Teaching Professor is responsible for coordinating, leading, and teaching courses in the MSN program. The NTTR MSN Faculty upholds academic integrity, follows standards of practice, and collaborates with the all MSN and SON faculty to ensure curriculum alignment with CCNE Essentials and the national standards applicable to the assigned track. The role supports graduate preparation for national certification eligibility in the PMHNP track, fosters program effectiveness, and promotes a student-centered, high-quality learning environment. ‌ Specific responsibilities include: Organizational Relationship: Workload assigned by the MSN Program Director and SON Director Evaluated annually by the Associate School Director and/or SON Director and with input from peer faculty Maintain regular, proactive communication with MSN Faculty and Program Director regarding course operations, student concerns, and any emerging issues, ensuring alignment with program expectations and timely resolution. Program Leadership: Actively engage in SON, MSN program, course, and university meetings, as designated by the SON Director and Associate Director/MSN Program director to support shared governance and program effectiveness. Collaborate regularly with other MSN Faculty to address MSN curriculum, course content, grading practices, student concerns, and faculty or university-related matters. Escalate unresolved issues to the MSN Program Director following appropriate communication pathways. Contribute to program success through participation in activities related to student admission, progression, and orientation, as well as curriculum review and enhancement for students enrolled in or applying to the MSN program. Ensure alignment with CCNE Standards, the national competencies applicable to AACN and NONPF competencies, and other professional standards as appropriate. Faculty Leadership: Maintain an active presence and engagement throughout the MSN program by monitoring responsiveness, grading practices, and interactions with students. Collaboratively review and discuss student assignments receiving a grade of 80% or below to ensure timely academic support and consistency in evaluation. Plan, teach, manage, and evaluate lectures and course activities while ensuring instructional excellence and innovation in content delivery. Review course materials, including readings, textbooks, and learning resources, to ensure alignment with current evidence-based practice, AACN Essentials, CCNE Standards, NONPF, and other professional standards as appropriate and communicate any necessary updates to the applicable MSN Track Coordinator(s) to maintain curricular relevance and accuracy. Collaborates closely with the MSN Program Director/Associate Director and MSN faculty to maintain the quality of courses and overall program effectiveness while fostering an enriching learning experience for students. Other duties include: Be accessible and available to students, supervisor, staff and colleagues during NKU operation hours (8:00 am – 4:30 pm EST). Serve on SON and program committees as assigned and attend SON, program, and other meetings in person or virtually; be an active participate in SON, program, and university needs. Education Doctoral degree in Nursing or related field required. Advanced Practice Certification as an PMHNP. Qualifications: Minimum of two years of clinical nursing practice required. Must possess an active and unencumbered registered nursing (RN) license in State of residence and an advanced practice license as an PMHNP At least three-years of full-time, past and current direct patient care as an PMHNP. Previous graduate- level teaching required Previous online teaching experience required Experience or expertise with course content Pass pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law Professional Expectations: Maintain active unencumbered RN licensure and, for APRN track positions, APRN certification/licensure Maintain current knowledge of professional discipline and educational methodologies through continuing professional development Maintain part-time clinical practice as needed to maintain APRN certification/licensure; ensure clinical practice (max release is one day weekly) does not interfere with faculty duties Maintain current knowledge of program policies, procedures, and student progress Adhere to faculty professional standards as delineated in the NKU Faculty Handbook Utilize nku.edu email for ALL course communications – students are required to do the same Teach and precept as needed to meet program needs Required Training: Completes ‘Best Practices for Online Teaching’ Canvas course as assigned Completes required Faculty Development courses annually Complete Clinical systems training currently used in program (i.e., Medatrax) Please include: RN license report (from NURSYS) APRN Certificate/License CV Teaching Philosophy Cover letter References ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Men-s-Tennis-Coach_JR100499": {
      "title": "Assistant Men's Tennis Coach",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Men's Tennis Coach ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Men’s Tennis Coach reports directly to the Head Men’s and Women’s Tennis Coach and is responsible for assisting the head coach with the organization and administration of the men’s tennis program in accordance with the rules and regulations of the University, Horizon League and NCAA. ‌ The Assistant Men’s Tennis Coach must have a commitment to developing a competitive NCAA Division I tennis program, while maintaining an emphasis on the academic success of the student-athlete. The Assistant Men’s Tennis Coach will be expected to administer the program in a manner that promotes the health, safety and welfare of the student-athlete. Compliance with NCAA rules is of the utmost importance at Northern Kentucky University. As a member of the athletics department staff, it is expected that the Assistant Men’s Tennis Coach will have a full understanding of the NCAA rules that pertain to the position. It is also expected that the Assistant Men’s Tennis Coach will comply with all NCAA rules and if he/she becomes aware, or have reasonable cause to believe, that a violation of a rule has occurred he/she will immediately report it to the Director of Athletics or his/her designee. Assist in the recruitment of student-athletes in accordance with NCAA regulations and academic standards, as well as University academic requirements.   Monitor the academics of the men’s tennis student-athletes.  Effectively communicate with Athletics Academic Advisor to ensure any academic concerns are being addressed.   Assist in the planning and coordination of in-season practices, including team and individual workouts.   Assist in the planning and coordination of out-of-season practices, including individual skill instruction and team workouts, focusing on the development of athletic skills to compete at the Division I level.   Assist in the planning and implementation of plans for each match, including travel to all conference away matches and travel to a majority of all non-conference away matches.   Complete all necessary compliance forms as required and/or requested by the Athletics Compliance Office.   Assist in scheduling matches as directed by Head Coach.   Monitor budget to ensure the men’s tennis program is fiscally responsible and expenditures are within the programs budget allocation as directed by the Head Coach.   Participate in fund raising activities for the men’s tennis program and/or Department of Athletics.   Attend Department of Athletics staff meetings and training as directed by the Director of Athletics. Bachelor's degree and previous tennis coaching experience required. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Partnerships-Manager--Norse-Network-Hub_JR100511-1": {
      "title": "Partnerships Manager, Norse Network Hub",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Partnerships Manager, Norse Network Hub ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: The Partnerships Manager serves as the primary liaison between community and business partners and the university, connecting external inquiries and collaboration opportunities with the right departments. This role manages workflows, timelines, and deliverables to ensure effective and timely engagement. The Manager also oversees partnership tracking through systems such as Raiser’s Edge, Handshake, and Team Dynamix. The ideal candidate is customer-focused, tech-savvy, and skilled in organization and project management. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Act as the primary point of contact for external stakeholders seeking collaboration opportunities with the university. Manage the process including meeting facilitation, summarization and communication of outcomes to relevant stakeholders and tracking within appropriate university systems. Assess and route partnership inquiries to the appropriate university Spoke, departments or personnel. Track, monitor, and follow up on inquiries to ensure that they are addressed and progressed appropriately. Develop and maintain efficient processes and data management for tracking and managing external engagement activities Support strategic initiatives related to university-community-business engagement. Collaborate with internal departments to support engagement initiatives and improve external stakeholder experiences. Customer relationship management to implement strategies to improve customer engagement Working with the Executive Director and partners across campus, implement and execute the Hub’s partnership model. Provide excellent customer service to ensure that objectives and timelines are met. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Bachelor’s degree in business administration, communications, higher education administration, or related filed. Have exceptional customer service, relationship management, and collaboration skills, with a proven ability to manage multiple projects, track progress, and ensure timely completion. Should be proficient in CRM and workflow systems such as Raiser’s Edge, Handshake, and Team Dynamix, and demonstrate strong technological aptitude with the ability to learn new systems quickly. Will be proactive and results-driven, with strong problem-solving abilities and the organizational awareness needed to navigate complex institutions effectively. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Tenure-Track-Assistant-Professor-of-Mechatronics-Engineering-Technology_JR100449": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Mechatronics Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Mechatronics Engineering Technology ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role:     The Department of Physics, Geology, and Engineering Technology (PGET) at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a tenure-track position in Mechatronics Engineering Technology to begin August 2027. ‌ The PGET department has 10 tenured/tenure-track faculty members and 4 full-time teaching faculty who serve approximately 260 students enrolled in its programs. The Engineering Technology program has three majors in Mechanical and Manufacturing Engineering Technology (MMET), Electrical and Electronics Engineering Technology (EEET), and Mechatronics Engineering Technology (MET). All three majors have recently been re-accredited by ABET (Accreditation Board for Engineering and Technology) through 2032. The entire Engineering Technology program will be relocated to the new expansion of the Herrmann Science Center in summer 2027. Our new colleague will be expected to contribute effectively in all three areas of professional responsibility at NKU: teaching, research, and service.  This includes teaching introductory and upper-level courses in the mechatronics engineering technology curricula with a student-centered focus, and enriching student experiences through involvement in co-curricular activities. In addition, our new colleague will be expected to conduct course assessment and continuous improvement activities. Undergraduate research opportunities are highly valued within the department, and faculty are expected to provide research experiences to undergraduate students by involving them in their own scholarship and mentoring capstone projects.  Our new colleague will also be expected to develop and cultivate relationships with employers in support of student professional development. Tenure-track faculty members also are expected to engage in service activities at all levels of the university. Research expertise or specialization in any area of mechatronics engineering technology will be considered, provided that it can support a productive research program at NKU, involve students, and contribute to the broader Northern Kentucky and Greater Cincinnati communities. Our new colleague will have opportunities to engage in K-12 outreach, participate in student recruitment, and help shape the future of the engineering technology program.      Responsibilities for this position include the following : Teach introductory and upper-level courses across the engineering technology curriculum, integrating hands-on lab activities into the classroom.  Improve the Mechatronics Engineering Technology curriculum, including developing undefined. Participate in ABET course assessment and continuous improvement activities. Establish and maintain a productive applied research program that engages NKU undergraduate students. Mentor undergraduate engineering technology capstone projects. Disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed journals and national and international conferences. Mentor students in their academic and professional development, including helping them identify research, internship, and other professional opportunities. Establish or expand professional connections in industrial, governmental, and academic communities.   Participate in service activities at the university, professional, and community levels. Required qualifications: Earned doctorate in a mechatronics-related engineering or engineering technology field, such as mechanical, manufacturing, electrical, electronics, or industrial engineering and/or engineering technology.  Demonstrated expertise through relevant academic and/or professional experience in one or more of the following areas, including but not limited to: integrated manufacturing systems; lean manufacturing; advanced industrial and/or collaborative (cobots) robotics integration; industrial control systems; or work-cell design. Commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and demonstrated ability to teach courses within the engineering technology and engineering physics programs. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain a productive applied research program in mechatronics engineering technology that engages undergraduate students. Record of peer-reviewed scholarly research in mechatronics-related engineering or engineering technology. Excellence in written and oral communication. Preferred qualifications: Effective teaching experience in introductory and advanced engineering technology courses. Relevant industry experience and/or a demonstrated track record of engagement with industry. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to supporting the needs of the student population served by NKU. Demonstrated involvement in student organizations. Prior involvement in K-12 outreach. All interested, qualified persons must apply for this position online at http://jobs.NKU.edu and will be asked to provide the following documents in PDF format. Cover letter outlining qualifications and interests Detailed curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research plan   Unofficial copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts List of three references with contact information The successful candidate will be required to undergo a pre-employment criminal background check as required by state law. Review of applications will begin on November 20, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Please contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Gang Sun ( sung1@nku.edu ), with any questions. ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Woodwinds_JR100497": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Woodwinds",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor, Woodwinds ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The School of the Arts at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for an Associate Teaching Professor position in one or more of the following applied areas; flute, clarinet, oboe or bassoon and Woodwind Area Coordinator within the Music Program, beginning Fall 2027. This position's main responsibilities are to teach a full undergraduate course load each semester (typically a combination of courses and applied lessons) and share curriculum oversight; maintain creative/ professional achievement; and service to the university and community.  As a NASM accredited program, teaching responsibilities adhere to loads as prescribed by NASM. The School of the Arts at Northern Kentucky University offers a wide array of degree programs in the visual and performing arts. The Music Program within the School of the Arts offers a BME in Music Education (Choral/Vocal and Instrumental), a BM in Performance (Instrumental, Jazz Studies, Piano Pedagogy, and Voice) a BM in Composition (Traditional Composition or Commercial Music Production) and a BA in Music (Liberal Studies). The Music Program is a fully accredited institutional member of the National Association of Schools of Music. See the Music web site at music.nku.edu for additional information. ‌ Job Details: Teach applied studio flute, oboe, clarinet, or bassoon Recruit and maintain a high-quality applied studio through teaching and performance activities. Coach woodwind chamber ensemble and other collaborative chamber music experiences Coordinate the Woodwind Area. Demonstrated ability and/or evidence to contribute effectively to one or more secondary areas. Secondary area teaching responsibilities may include music theory, music history, aural skills, woodwind methods or other courses as assigned. The Music Program is open to innovative and broad skill sets that may benefit our program in unexpected ways. In the applied area, evidence of effective applied teaching and mentoring of students should be present. Successful recruitment and retention in the private applied studio are an important point of consideration. Applicants should demonstrate a commitment to student-centered teaching and to creating a supportive learning environment for students with varied backgrounds, experiences, and professional goals. Qualifications: Applicants should either possess a Doctorate in Music or a Master of Music degree with commensurate  exceptional experience. Applicants should either possess a Doctorate in Music or a Master of Music degree with commensurate  exceptional experience. Successful applicants will demonstrate the potential for a successful career in teaching and for sustained engagement in professional Evidence ofongoing professional, creative, pedagogical, and/or scholarly  engagement appropriate to the position is required. Successful teaching at the university level (at least two years preferred) and sustained experience as a solo and ensemble performer is required. The candidate must remain current within the music discipline and apply continued knowledge towards course instruction, provide mentorship along with fellow faculty to music students, maintain office hours to be accessible to students and staff, submit mid-term and final grades according to University deadlines, and work cooperatively with all SOTA faculty. Application: Questions regarding the use of this website should be directed to the Human Resources Department at jobs@nku.edu . Questions regarding the nature of the position should be directed to the search committee chair, Mr. William Brian Hogg.   Candidates should submit materials electronically through Northern Kentucky University’s website portal jobs.nku.edu. Required materials include: 1.    Letter of application 2.    Current curriculum vitae 3.    Teaching Philosophy. (Can be general to teaching or specific to the applied area) 4.    List of three references with phone numbers and email addresses. 5.    Link to performance video(s) 6.    Link to teaching video(s).   ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Teaching-Professor-in-Construction-Management_JR100481": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Construction Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Teaching Professor in Construction Management ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Department of Marketing, Sports Business & Construction Management in the Haile College of Business at Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a non-tenure-track, full-time Assistant Teaching Professor, to begin Spring 2027 (Fall 2027 considered). ‌ The successful candidate will:   develop course material aligned with ACCE accreditation standards teach a full undergraduate load of eight sections annually contribute to service commitments participate in construction management industry advisory board meetings attend employment/career fairs support the recruitment of students and potential future colleagues.  Active involvement in the life of the College and the university – including attendance at program, department, and college meetings – and continued involvement in the construction industry outside the university are expected. Qualifications   Preferred candidates will hold a Master’s degree in Construction Management, Civil Engineering, Architecture, or a closely related field at the time of appointment.  Candidates with an undergraduate degree in Construction Management and a Master of Business Administration (M.B.A.) will also be considered.  The candidate should have at least 10 years of direct experience in the construction industry and be able to develop course material aligned with accreditation standards and teach undergraduate courses. Teaching topics for consideration include construction management, construction safety, building codes, mechanical and electrical systems for construction, structural analysis, estimating, scheduling, land planning and development, construction layout, and heavy/civil construction.  Additional areas will be considered based on the individual’s background. OSHA certification or the demonstrated ability and willingness to obtain it is preferred, to support instruction in Construction Safety.     Application Documents (Required)   Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three references Statement of Teaching Philosophy   Minimum / Preferred Education   Minimum: Master’s Degree.  Preferred: Master’s Degree.   Review / Timeline   Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Open until filled.   Search Committee Chair (contact)   Majed Dabdoub - dabdoubm@nku.edu   Background Check   Any candidate offered this position will be required to complete a pre-employment criminal background check as mandated by state law.   ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Associate-Vice-President--Financial-Services_JR100506": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President, Financial Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Associate Vice President, Financial Services ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Associate Vice President for Financial Services (AVP) is a senior financial executive and the University’s lead leader for accounting and financial operations. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Administration and Finance/Chief Financial Officer (VP/CFO), the AVP provides strategic and operational leadership across a broad portfolio of financial functions and serves as a key advisor and partner to the CFO. Because the VP/CFO’s portfolio extends beyond finance to include Facilities, Human Resources, Information Technology, University Police, and Business and Auxiliary Services, the AVP has significant responsibility and autonomy for the day-to-day leadership of the University’s financial operations. The AVP also serves as the primary deputy for the Division of Administration and Finance in the VP/CFO’s absence. ‌ The Opportunity The next AVP will join the University at an important and exciting point in its financial evolution. The position inherits a strong foundation, including a longstanding record of external audits with no findings, two consecutive years of strengthened financial results, and the recent implementation of Workday Financials. The opportunity ahead is not simply to maintain that foundation, but to build upon it. The successful candidate will lead an experienced team of directors and managers, strengthen financial planning and reporting, and help the University realize the full potential of its investment in Workday. This leader will have the opportunity to modernize processes, reduce unnecessary manual work, strengthen data and reporting capabilities, and create a financial services organization known for both strong stewardship and excellent service. The AVP regularly engages with the Executive Leadership Team, President’s Cabinet, Board of Regents and its committees, academic and administrative leaders, auditors, financial institutions, and other stakeholders. The position requires a finance leader who can move comfortably between technical accounting matters, institutional strategy, operational leadership, and executive-level communication. The Office of Financial Services includes Budget, General Accounting, Grants and Contracts, Procurement, Accounts Payable, Treasury and Investment Management, Student Account Services, Tax Compliance, Inventory Control, Foundation Fiscal Management and Accounting, and related financial functions. Key Leadership Responsibilities Lead the Financial Services Organization Provide strategic and operational leadership for the Office of Financial Services. Lead, develop, and support directors and managers across the University’s financial functions; establish priorities and expectations; align resources with institutional needs; and ensure effective, responsive financial operations. Develop People and Build Organizational Capacity Recruit, develop, and retain a high-performing finance team. Coach and develop leaders, strengthen cross-training and succession depth, and foster a culture characterized by integrity, accountability, transparency, collaboration, documentation, and service. Advance Workday Financials Lead the continued optimization of Workday Financials following implementation. Partner with Information Technology, functional leaders, and Workday support resources to improve business processes, configuration, security, reporting, and adoption. Help transform Workday from a newly implemented system into a platform that provides efficient processes and timely, reliable information for decision-making. Drive Process Improvement and Modernization Evaluate financial processes across the University and identify opportunities to simplify work, automate appropriate activities, reduce manual effort, improve service, and strengthen controls. Build a culture of continuous improvement while maintaining appropriate financial stewardship and accountability. Ensure Excellence in Accounting and Financial Reporting Direct the preparation of the University’s annual financial statements, state reporting, interim financial reporting, and other financial information for executive leadership and the Board of Regents. Maintain disciplined month-end and year-end close processes and ensure accurate and timely financial reporting for the University and its Foundation. Lead Audit, Compliance, and Internal Controls Serve as the primary day-to-day liaison with internal and external auditors and lead the annual external audit process. Partner with the VP/CFO in establishing, interpreting, and monitoring fiscal policies and internal controls. Sustain the University’s strong audit record while ensuring assets are appropriately safeguarded and financial practices remain compliant. Provide Technical Accounting Leadership Ensure accounting structures, including the University’s chart of accounts within Workday, support accurate financial reporting and effective institutional decision-making. Ensure compliance with GAAP, GASB standards, and applicable state and federal requirements. Lead implementation of new accounting standards and oversee areas including tax compliance, grants and contracts accounting, fixed assets, and inventory control. Lead Budget and Financial Planning Provide leadership to the Budget Office and partner with the VP/CFO on annual and multi-year financial planning, forecasting, budget development, monitoring, and analysis. Help translate financial information into actionable insights that support institutional priorities and long-term financial sustainability. Oversee Treasury, Cash, Investments, and Debt Provide executive oversight of cash management, cash-flow forecasting, institutional investments, banking relationships, and payment obligations. Ensure compliance with debt and bond covenants, investment policies, and related financial requirements. Oversee Student Account Services Provide leadership for student billing, accounts receivable, and collections, balancing sound financial practices with accurate, responsive, and student-focused service. Oversee Procurement and Accounts Payable Provide leadership for procurement and accounts payable operations, ensuring efficient processes, appropriate internal controls, regulatory compliance, and strong service to the University community. Serve as Deputy to the VP/CFO Serve as the primary deputy for the Division of Administration and Finance in the VP/CFO’s absence. Represent Financial Services with executive leadership and the Board of Regents and its committees, presenting complex financial information in a clear, accurate, transparent, and decision-useful manner. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a closely related field. Active Certified Public Accountant (CPA) license. At least 10 years of progressively responsible accounting and finance experience, including significant leadership responsibility and at least five years leading managers, directors, or comparable professional teams. Demonstrated expertise in financial accounting and reporting, GAAP, internal controls, and external audit management. Demonstrated success developing teams and leaders, including hiring, coaching, performance management, and organizational development. Experience leading significant process improvement, modernization, or organizational change within a complex financial environment. Experience with enterprise financial systems and demonstrated ability to use technology, data, and reporting to improve financial operations and decision-making. Strong executive communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to explain complex financial information clearly to both financial and non-financial audiences. Demonstrated ability to collaborate across organizational boundaries and influence decisions in a complex organization. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, or a related field. Senior financial leadership experience in higher education, government, or another complex public-sector environment. Knowledge of GASB accounting and reporting standards. Experience with Workday Financials, particularly implementation, stabilization, or post-implementation optimization. Experience with institutional budgeting and financial planning, treasury and investment management, debt compliance, or banking relationships. Experience presenting financial information to governing boards or comparable executive-level stakeholders. Experience with financial reporting, analytics, or business intelligence tools. Additional relevant professional credentials, such as Certified Government Financial Manager (CGFM) or Certified Management Accountant (CMA). The Leader We Are Seeking The successful candidate will be both a strong technical finance professional and an effective organizational leader. They will understand that excellence in financial services is measured not only by accurate statements and clean audits, but also by the quality of the team, the effectiveness of business processes, the usefulness of financial information, and the experience of the people the organization serves. This individual will bring sound judgment, intellectual curiosity, a commitment to continuous improvement, and the confidence to challenge existing practices when a better approach is available. They will be comfortable operating at both the strategic and operational levels—able to discuss institutional financial strategy with executive leadership and the Board while also understanding the processes, systems, controls, and people required to execute that strategy successfully. Above all, the AVP will be a trusted financial leader who values transparency, accountability, collaboration, and responsible stewardship of University resources. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Mostly indoor office work. Some occasional light lifting may be necessary."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Coordinator--HR---Compensation---Benefits_JR100527": {
      "title": "Coordinator, HR - Compensation & Benefits",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Coordinator, HR - Compensation & Benefits ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Compensation and Benefits Coordinator supports the administration of the university's compensation, classification, benefits, and HRIS programs. This position is responsible for processing and maintaining employee, position, compensation, and benefits data; supporting salary administration and annual enrollment activities; preparing reports and audits; and providing customer service to employees and departments regarding HR processes and programs. ‌ Join NKU's Human Resources team and play a key role in supporting compensation, benefits, and HR operations. In this position, you will: Maintain and update position, job, compensation, and benefits data in Workday and related systems. Support compensation and classification processes, including position changes, reclassifications, salary administration, and market reviews. Coordinate and participate in salary surveys, job matching, and compensation data collection. Process employee benefits enrollments, life events, eligibility changes, and other benefits-related transactions. Review, audit, and reconcile HR, compensation, and benefits data to ensure accuracy and compliance. Prepare reports and analyses that support compensation, benefits, and workforce decision-making. Assist with annual processes such as salary increases, open enrollment, system testing, and HR data validation. Respond to employee and department questions regarding compensation, benefits, and HR processes. Partner with HR colleagues, campus departments, and external vendors to resolve issues and improve service delivery. We're seeking a detail-oriented HR professional who enjoys working with data, systems, and people. The successful candidates will have: Two or more years of experience supporting HR operations, benefits, compensation, HRIS, payroll, or similar functions. Bachelor's degree preferred in a related field Experience working with HR data, reporting, records, and business systems. Strong proficiency in Microsoft Excel and other Microsoft Office applications. Experience using Workday or another enterprise HRIS. Excellent analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Strong customer service and communication skills. Ability to manage confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Experience working in higher education or another complex organization. Join NKU's Human Resources team and develop expertise in compensation, benefits, and HR systems. The Compensation and Benefits Coordinator supports key employee programs through HRIS administration, compensation and benefits processing, reporting, data analysis, and customer service. Working in higher education provides a unique opportunity to combine a rewarding HR career with meaningful work that supports the faculty, staff, and students who shape the future of our region and beyond. Please provide a resume, cover letter and references ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Grant-Administrator-I_JR100518": {
      "title": "Grant Administrator I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Grant Administrator I ‌ Position Type: Fixed Term (Fixed Term) ‌ About the Role: This position provides assistance to faculty/staff and to Research, Grants & Contracts staff in the development and preparation of grant and contract proposals and awards from external funders. The Grant Administrator 1 will utilize electronic systems to conduct research in support of grant proposals. The Grant Administrator 1 will also assist faculty/staff in developing proposals and budgets, submit proposals on behalf of faculty/staff at NKU, assist other staff in the RGC office with grant related tasks as needed to gain new knowledge, and participate in sponsored research initiatives and projects as assigned. This is an entry-level position. ‌ Provides support to RGC office in reviewing proposals, submitting proposals, and researching available external funding opportunities. Review and confirm compliance requirements for proposals and awards. Assist in planning and executing grant workshops, seminars and other RGC signature events throughout the year Minimum bachelor’s degree with 2 years of related experience. Must be computer literate with the ability and willingness to continuously learn new electronic software systems for the submittal and awarding of grant proposals. Please provide a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: $21 per hour ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Temporary-Candidate-Pool_JR100536": {
      "title": "Temporary Candidate Pool",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Temporary Candidate Pool ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University is accepting applications for temporary staff opportunities across various departments. Temporary assignments may support operational, administrative, technical, customer service, programmatic, or project-based needs. Positions may be part-time or full-time and are generally established to meet short-term staffing requirements. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Duties will vary based on departmental needs and may include: Providing administrative and operational support Assisting with projects, events, or special initiatives Delivering customer service and stakeholder support Maintaining records and documentation Supporting departmental programs and daily operations Performing other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Ability to effectively communicate and work with a diverse population Basic computer proficiency Ability to perform assigned duties with minimal supervision Preferred Qualifications Relevant education, training, or experience related to the assignment Previous experience in a professional, higher education, or customer service environment Additional Information This posting is intended to create a temporary applicant pool for current and anticipated short-term staffing needs. Assignments may vary in duration, schedule, responsibilities, and compensation based on departmental requirements. Applicants will be considered for temporary opportunities as they become available. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Specialist--Service_JR100510": {
      "title": "Specialist, Service",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Specialist, Service ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University welcomes applications for the position of Registrar Services Coordinator in the Office of the Registrar. This position serves as a primary resource for students, faculty, staff, and external constituents seeking assistance with academic records, registration, enrollment verification, transcript services, and university policies and procedures. The Registrar Services Coordinator is responsible for providing exceptional customer service, maintaining the integrity of academic records, and supporting student information system operations. This role requires extensive knowledge of university policies, academic regulations, registration processes, and student records management while serving as a key liaison between the Registrar's Office and the campus community. ‌ Primary Responsibilities Student and Customer Support Serve as the primary point of contact for walk-in visitors, telephone inquiries, and electronic communications received by the Office of the Registrar. Assist students with services including transcript requests, enrollment verifications, registration support, academic record updates, and demographic changes. Provide guidance regarding university policies, procedures, and academic requirements. Direct students and visitors to appropriate campus resources for matters related to transfer credit, academic renewal, financial aid, residency, veterans benefits, and other specialized services. Respond to inquiries from students, parents, faculty, staff, administrators, and external agencies. Troubleshoot registration issues and assist with resolving enrollment barriers, advising holds, prerequisite restrictions, registration windows, and course enrollment concerns. Provide supervision, training, and daily guidance to student employees supporting front-line operations. Academic Records Administration Process and maintain student academic records with a high degree of accuracy and confidentiality. Perform data entry and record maintenance within the student information system. Audit, update, and verify academic records to ensure compliance with university policies and procedures. Process program changes and other record updates affecting student academic standing and GPA calculations. Research and respond to requests for information regarding academic records from internal and external stakeholders. Monitor reports and identify discrepancies requiring correction or follow-up action. Systems Support and Process Improvement Assist with identifying business requirements and system enhancements within the student information system. Participate in system testing, upgrades, patches, and implementation activities to ensure functionality and data integrity. Identify and assist in resolving data and system issues. Support training efforts related to new and enhanced system functionality. Maintain proficiency in student information systems, Microsoft Office applications, and other technologies required to support office operations. Minimum Qualifications Associate's degree and two years of related administrative, customer service, records management, higher education, or student services experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience providing customer service in a fast-paced environment. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate and confidential records. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated organizational, problem-solving, and analytical abilities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree. Experience working in a college or university environment. Experience with student information systems such as SAP or Workday Knowledge of FERPA and academic records management practices. Experience training or supervising student employees. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to interpret and apply complex policies, procedures, and academic regulations. Strong commitment to providing exceptional customer service. Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Ability to research, analyze, and resolve issues independently. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders. Strong technical aptitude and willingness to learn new systems and processes. This position offers the opportunity to play an important role in supporting student success by ensuring the accuracy, accessibility, and integrity of academic records and registration services. Please upload a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Assistant-Director-of-Donor-Engagement_JR100477": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Donor Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Assistant Director of Donor Engagement ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Assistant Director of Donor Engagement contributes to NKU’s fundraising success by designing and coordinating donor experiences and connections to the impact of their giving. This position is an instrumental part of University Advancement, ensuring donors receive timely thank you messages and are regularly engaged. ‌ Coordinate opportunities for donors to experience and understand the impact of their giving such as storytelling, donor/beneficiary connections, and other unique events, reports, and touchpoints that connect them to their philanthropy.   Coordinate and execute the acknowledgment process, including routing, personalizing, and sending acknowledgments to donors to properly and promptly thank them for their gifts, as well as regularly reviewing and refreshing acknowledgment content. In collaboration with other areas of University Advancement, coordinate customized donor programs, including various giving societies, to ensure we recognize donors’ special moments, milestones, and behavior.  Manage various donor relations events throughout the year. Maintain in-depth knowledge of university priorities, programs, and initiatives to identify ongoing engagement opportunities for donors and prospects, including those within an assigned stewardship portfolio. Provide administrative support for donor visits and general donor relations operations, including packaging and mailing donor gifts, managing communications, and coordinating outreach. Maintain NKU’s donor database related to donor relations, ensuring touchpoints and outreach are captured accurately and kept up-to-date. Maintain a resource that identifies on-campus engagement and giving opportunities to share with donors and friends as well as University Advancement staff Bachelor's degree and 2 years of related work experience required. Candidate must have: Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines effectively Excellent written and verbal communication skills Creativity and problem-solving skills Ability to work collaboratively Commitment to the mission and vision of Northern Kentucky University High ethical standards Proficiency in Microsoft Office suite and donor management software (Raiser’s Edge) preferred Please include a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: Some weekend/evening work is required"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Associate-Director--Technology_JR100532": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Associate Director, Technology ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: The Associate Director of Technology is a member of the Office of Student Financial Assistance and reports to the Assistant Vice President of Financial Assistance and Operations. This position manages and improves the technology infrastructure and systems for financial aid operations, ensuring compliance and efficient aid delivery. This position will provide technical managerial leadership and oversee all departmental systems, technology and data activities. The Associate Director of Technology will be responsible for directing a team of professionals and managing complex projects to streamline data analysis workflows, resolving system issues and collaborating with IT and other campus colleagues to ensure efficient financial aid awarding to enhance student success. The Associate Director Technology will identify opportunities to maximize the use of technology to provide funding, tools and information necessary for awarding aid to students. The position will ensure that our systems a build to meet compliance requirements with efficiencies for students, faculty and staff. The Associate Director of Technology will play a key role in coordinating the implementation of new and modernized business system solutions. This position will serve as a liaison to external vendors or partners in support of business systems, which may include the development, implementation and /or operations. The Associate Director of Technology will be responsible for performing and coordinating system testing for new and existing system applications, with includes upgrades and patching of existing systems; planning, conducting and documenting results of testing (managing the department’s testing). ‌ M anaging and maintain all financial aid technologies and business solutions. Developing instructional technical materials and conduct training. Translating business processes into system requirements and/or development of system solutions. Analyzing new business requirements and determine the best way to utilize system resources to comply with requirement(s). Analyze data and support data request. Assist the office and campus partners in solving complex problems or issues regarding management of business systems. Review, research and evaluate software solutions to determine usefulness, benefits and opportunities to support and enhance student success. Masters degree and 4 years of related experience required Working knowledge of Title IV regulations. Knowledge of computer system capabilities, business processes and workflow. Ability to conduct training on technologies. Ability to problem solve and think analytically to identify optimal business system solutions.    Please attach a resume, cover letter and references. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Specialist--Student-Financial-Assistance_JR100533": {
      "title": "Specialist, Student Financial Assistance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Specialist, Student Financial Assistance ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a Processing Specialist within the Office of Student Financial Assistance. This position serves as a key operational role supporting student-facing services by processing a variety of transactions and maintaining accurate student records across multiple functional areas, including student accounts, and registration-related services. ‌ The Processing Specialist works collaboratively with campus partners to ensure efficient, accurate, and timely processing while supporting a seamless student experience. Primary Responsibilities Provide front-line or tiered support to students and families by responding to inquiries via in-person, phone, and electronic communication channels Collaborate with functional areas (One Stop, Registrar, Student Account Services, Admissions) to ensure consistent and accurate service delivery Process student-related transactions and records in accordance with university policies and federal/state regulations (e.g., financial aid, billing, registration support, and general student services) Review documentation for completeness and accuracy; resolve discrepancies and follow up with students or campus partners as needed Maintain data integrity across university systems by entering, updating, and auditing information Maintain confidentiality of student records in compliance with FERPA and university policies Support continuous improvement efforts by identifying process inefficiencies and recommending enhancements   Qualifications High school diploma or GED required; post-secondary education (1–2 years of college or equivalent coursework) preferred Minimum of 1–2 years of experience in an administrative, customer service, or data-processing environment Excellent customer service and communication skills Strong attention to detail and ability to manage high-volume transactional work accurately Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to handle multiple priorities High level of accuracy, discretion, and professionalism Ability to work both independently and as part of a team   Why Join NKU Northern Kentucky University is a student-ready, regionally focused institution committed to delivering high-quality, student-centered services. The Office of Student Financial Assistance plays a critical role in simplifying processes and improving the student experience. ‌ Posted Salary: $16.74 per hour ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Specialist--Student-Financial-Assistance_JR100534": {
      "title": "Specialist, Student Financial Assistance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Specialist, Student Financial Assistance ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: Northern Kentucky University invites applications for a Processing Specialist within Financial Assistance. This position plays a critical role in supporting the administration of federal, state, institutional financial aid and foundation/donor funded programs through accurate processing, record maintenance, compliance review, and student support. The Processing Specialist works collaboratively with students, families, campus partners, and external agencies to ensure efficient service delivery and adherence to regulatory requirements. ‌ The Processing Specialist supports financial aid operations by processing student aid records, reviewing documentation, maintaining compliance with federal and state regulations, and assisting students throughout the financial aid lifecycle. This position also provides season support to foundation donor funded aid processing. This position requires strong attention to detail, customer service skills, and the ability to manage high-volume transactional work in a fast-paced environment. Primary Responsibilities Process financial aid transactions, records, and documentation in accordance with federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies. Review financial aid applications, verification materials, and supporting documentation for completeness, accuracy, and compliance. Maintain and update student records within university systems, ensuring data integrity and regulatory compliance. Monitor and resolve discrepancies related to financial aid eligibility, packaging, awards, and student records. Communicate with students, families, and campus partners regarding financial aid requirements, processes, and deadlines through in-person, phone, email, and virtual channels. Assist in the administration of federal, state, institutional, and scholarship aid programs. Support processing activities related to verification, satisfactory academic progress, professional judgment, dependency overrides, and other aid eligibility determinations, as assigned. Collaborate with colleagues and campus partners (Admissions, Student Account Services the Registrar's Office, and other university offices) to provide coordinated student support. Participate in peak processing periods and assist with special projects, audits, reporting requirements, and compliance reviews. Identify opportunities for process improvement and support implementation of efficiencies that enhance service and operational effectiveness. Maintain confidentiality of student information in accordance with FERPA and applicable regulations. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or GED required. Two years of experience in administrative support, records processing, compliance, customer service, financial aid, higher education, or a related field. Experience working with computerized information systems and data entry processes. Demonstrated attention to detail and ability to accurately process high-volume transactions. Preferred Qualifications Associate's or Bachelor's degree. Experience working in financial aid, student services, higher education, banking, insurance, compliance, or a similarly regulated environment. Knowledge of federal financial aid regulations and programs. Experience using student information systems, Workday, Banner, or related enterprise systems. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to interpret and apply policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements. Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities. Commitment to providing exceptional customer service. Ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and electronic record systems. Why Join NKU Northern Kentucky University is a student-ready, regionally engaged institution committed to transforming lives through education. Financial Assistance plays a vital role in helping students access and afford a college education. This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact by supporting student success while ensuring responsible stewardship of financial aid resources. ‌ Posted Salary: $16.74 per hour ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/NKU-Music-Preparatory-Teaching-Staff_JR100227": {
      "title": "NKU Music Preparatory Teaching Staff",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: NKU Music Preparatory Teaching Staff ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: NKU Music Preparatory Teaching Staff ‌ The NKU Music Preparatory Program is dedicated to making high-quality music education accessible to learners of all ages, backgrounds, and abilities. We believe that the arts are a vital part of a thriving community and a fundamental element of personal growth. Through exceptional instruction, innovative programming, and meaningful community engagement, NKU Music Prep enriches the cultural life of the Northern Kentucky and Greater Cincinnati region. NKU Music Prep has an ongoing need for teachers with expertise in all instruments and voice for private lesson instruction, as well as teachers for classroom instruction. For a complete list of current Music Prep offerings, visit the NKU Music Prep website.  Music Prep staff teach weekly lessons or classes depending on their expertise and assignment. Pay is determined by enrollment (private lesson students), time commitment (class instructor), and experience. This is an open application for our candidate pool. We are accepting applications from qualified candidates for future opportunities. While there may not be an immediate opening, applications will be reviewed and retained for consideration as positions become available. ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Academic-Coordinator---School-of-Social-Work_JR100540": {
      "title": "Academic Coordinator - School of Social Work",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nPosition Title: Academic Coordinator - School of Social Work ‌ Position Type: Regular ‌ About the Role: This position provides comprehensive administrative support to the School of Social Work (SSW) and its academic programs. Responsibilities include supporting the school’s financial management, accounts payable, billing, and reporting functions, as well as providing dedicated administrative and academic support to the programs housed within the SSW. ‌ ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Administrative Support of New Hire Process, Faculty Credentialing, and Personnel Documentation/Processes. Responsible for processing confidential pay & personnel (PAPS, etc.) Responsible for setting up faculty/instructor data & credentialing materials in Faculty Success. Support GA hiring for the SSW. Oversight for confidential departmental, student, and faculty files. Responsible for processing Separation PAPs and related paperwork/ electronic inputs for Faculty & Staff positions. College recruitment and event support. External partners support. Support other responsibilities as needed. Administrative support of Financial Management, Bill Pay, and Reporting Functions. Responsible for general financial management functions, including grants and foundation accounts. Responsible for processing Travel Requests and Expense Reports, Purchasing Supplies and reconciling ProCards, and Time Administration. Ensures compliance with all NKU guidelines. Key Designee for SSW (Key requests, returns, audits, etc.) Responsible for directly or as the backup resource for bill payment, purchase requisitions, budget transfers, revenue transfers, vendor setup, revenue collection & bursar deposits, reconciliation of accounts, and other financial administration related duties. Responsible for and assist the Business Officer with SSW reporting. Responsible directly or as the backup resource for the coordination of grant accounts and associated paperwork with faculty and other CHHS Staff. Oversight of departmental equipment/ furniture/ computer inventory (including annual reconciliations, tagging, and upgrade/replacement processes). Support other responsibilities as needed.   KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: General business and computer skills, with proficiency in MS Office Suite (especially Excel), Adobe, and Canva. SAP and Workday experience is helpful, yet not mandatory. Requires good time management, basic math skills, interpersonal and communication skills, as well as the ability to adapt to change quickly. Additional competencies include strong data skills/management and attention to detail.   EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: Bachelor’s Degree and 2 years of work experience ‌ Posted Salary: Minimum $19.04/hr ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands: ​​Indoor desk work​. Walking, occasionally lifting of boxes, and delivery and restocking of supplies."
    },
    "https://nku.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/NKU_External/job/Highland-Heights-Ky/Norse-Violence-Prevention-Back-up-Advocate_JR100541": {
      "title": "Norse Violence Prevention Back-up Advocate",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nPosition Title: Norse Violence Prevention Back-up Advocate ‌ Position Type: Temporary ‌ About the Role: The Back-up Advocate will provide victim advocacy services on an as needed basis to ensure advocacy coverage in the Norse Violence Prevention office. This position is part-time and will report as needed out of the Norse Violence Prevention Center. The position serves students impacted by interpersonal violence including sexual assault, relationship violence, and/or stalking and is responsible for providing support services that are trauma-informed. Services include safety planning, crisis intervention, information and support with reporting options both on and off campus, academic and housing accommodations, general support services, and other services as needed. The Norse Violence Prevention (NVP) Back-up Advocate will work collaboratively with other departments and offices on campus (The Office of Title IX, Community Standards and Care, University Housing, University Police, and others) as well as with off campus systems (hospitals, courts, law enforcement) to support student survivors. The NVP Back-up Advocate is responsible for maintaining client confidentiality, maintaining appropriate documentation of services and providing all necessary information for grant reporting requirements. ‌ Responsibilities: Direct advocacy services to students (90%) Documentation of service and administrative tasks (10%)   Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in social work, counseling, psychology or other human services degree preferred. At least one year experience of advocacy and/or prevention required, preferably in a higher education setting. Demonstrated understanding of dynamics of interpersonal violence required. Please attach a resume ‌ Posted Salary: ‌ Work Environment & Physical Demands:"
    }
  },
